1
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:12,780
We're going to betray them?

2
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:14,120
With whom did he team up
after betraying me?

3
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:15,490
My gosh.

4
00:00:15,690 --> 00:00:17,490
Sang Min, you have a long way to go.

5
00:00:18,790 --> 00:00:20,990
I don't expect it from others.
But shouldn't you at least tell me?

6
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:24,330
Good work.

7
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:27,330
This isn't right.

8
00:00:27,330 --> 00:00:28,630
It's 27.53 million dollars.

9
00:00:29,170 --> 00:00:30,240
Oh, my. This is crazy.

10
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:31,540
Darn it.

11
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:32,540
Good job.

12
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:33,570
Sang Min!

13
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:34,640
- That's it.
- I won't pull.

14
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:35,710
That hurts. Darn it.

15
00:00:41,650 --> 00:00:43,380
You've completed 100,000 combos.

16
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:44,380
I did it.

17
00:00:47,350 --> 00:00:48,790
You can't make me crack up.
I'm on your team.

18
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:50,960
(Cop)

19
00:00:51,990 --> 00:00:53,020
Successfully...

20
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:57,630
My gosh, Tae Gyun. I thought you'd do it.

21
00:00:57,630 --> 00:01:00,060
Come on. What a way to ruin the game.

22
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:01,830
Did we mess up? No. They did.

23
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:03,540
They don't get it at all.

24
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:04,870
- I got it.
- I got it.

25
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:06,400
- I got it.
- I got it.

26
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:08,370
- I got it.
- Come on.

27
00:01:08,770 --> 00:01:09,840
Soldering.

28
00:01:10,210 --> 00:01:12,010
Keun Woo is on fire.

29
00:01:12,010 --> 00:01:13,210
- Gosh.
- Seriously.

30
00:01:13,210 --> 00:01:15,080
I think Ji Hoo just beat me.

31
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:16,820
It's anyone's game down to the wire.

32
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:18,920
All the games have ended.

33
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:20,650
You know what?
They're trying to confuse us.

34
00:01:20,650 --> 00:01:22,050
- Sang Min.
- I'm right. Admit it.

35
00:01:22,050 --> 00:01:23,190
That's the only justification.

36
00:01:23,190 --> 00:01:24,460
- Pure-bloods should team up.
- Yes.

37
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:26,830
I really liked my team best.

38
00:01:26,830 --> 00:01:29,160
- Rookie, Rookie, Rookie, yes!
- Rookie, Rookie, Rookie, yes!

39
00:01:29,190 --> 00:01:32,660
(And four players remain.)

40
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:43,070
I came with the goal to keep winning
in a way...

41
00:01:43,070 --> 00:01:44,380
that satisfied me.

42
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:46,210
(Heo Seong Beom)

43
00:01:46,210 --> 00:01:49,510
I want to win every single game
in front of me.

44
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:50,920
(YunB)

45
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:53,350
I fought tooth and nail to survive.

46
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:55,750
Surviving by any means necessary...

47
00:01:55,750 --> 00:01:57,720
is true strength.

48
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:00,630
I guess I have
a way of betraying people...

49
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:02,960
without getting on their bad side.

50
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,530
I felt lucky to be here every day.

51
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:07,400
I'll lean into that luck
a little more today.

52
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,200
(Kang Ji Hoo)

53
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:11,700
I'll use everything I've got
and won't give up to the end.

54
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,570
I'll beat the rest of them.

55
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:18,340
Hello.

56
00:02:18,940 --> 00:02:21,510
Four of you have made it
to the final match.

57
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:24,180
Welcome.

58
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:27,920
The final match consists
of three rounds...

59
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:30,120
in a 1-on-1 tournament.

60
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:34,490
The winners of Round 1 and Round 2...

61
00:02:34,830 --> 00:02:37,900
will advance to Round Three.

62
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:39,700
The winner of Round Three...

63
00:02:40,230 --> 00:02:43,270
will become the final winner
of Bloody Game X.

64
00:02:45,270 --> 00:02:46,570
Your final match opponent,
paired based on the results...

65
00:02:46,570 --> 00:02:49,040
of the semifinal match will be revealed.

66
00:02:49,370 --> 00:02:50,910
Round One of the final match...

67
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:53,210
will be between Kang Ji Hoo
in first place...

68
00:02:53,550 --> 00:02:56,050
and Hyun Sung Joo in fourth place.

69
00:02:56,780 --> 00:02:58,520
Round Two of the final match...

70
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:00,390
will be between YunB in second place...

71
00:03:00,750 --> 00:03:03,250
and Heo Seong Beom in third place.

72
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:08,090
The games for the final match
will be revealed.

73
00:03:09,630 --> 00:03:12,600
Pyramid Number. Card Chess.

74
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:14,500
Choice Hold'em.

75
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:16,940
The player with a higher rank...

76
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:19,770
from the semifinal match
will choose the game for the round.

77
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:24,210
By default, the unchosen game
will be set for Round Three.

78
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:26,840
Which one do you want to play?

79
00:03:28,650 --> 00:03:29,850
You'll pick the one I want?

80
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:31,720
No.

81
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,450
- You'll pick the one I don't want, right?
- Yes.

82
00:03:34,990 --> 00:03:36,420
I bet you want to go with Choice Hold'em.

83
00:03:38,390 --> 00:03:39,390
Yes.

84
00:03:40,260 --> 00:03:42,160
I wanted to go with Choice Hold'em
out of the three.

85
00:03:43,730 --> 00:03:44,960
But I was in fourth place.

86
00:03:45,930 --> 00:03:47,030
The decision wasn't up to me.

87
00:03:47,170 --> 00:03:50,400
I thought
I'd never be able to play that game.

88
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:52,870
Ji Hoo, you won first place
in the semifinal match.

89
00:03:53,070 --> 00:03:55,670
Go to the Voting Room. And select a game.

90
00:03:57,610 --> 00:03:58,680
Pyramid Number?

91
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,350
Card Chess?

92
00:04:02,250 --> 00:04:03,880
Sung Joo is...

93
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:06,180
number one Hold'em player in Korea.

94
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,020
I excluded that from my options.

95
00:04:08,490 --> 00:04:09,820
I had to choose between...

96
00:04:10,390 --> 00:04:12,520
Pyramid Number and Card Chess.

97
00:04:14,690 --> 00:04:16,760
Honestly,
I can beat anyone at a chess game.

98
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:20,670
Even Jang Dong Min can't beat me
at a chess game.

99
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,770
(Pyramid Number, Card Chess,
Choice Hold'em)

100
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:30,010
Ji Hoo, please select the game
for the final match.

101
00:04:30,510 --> 00:04:33,040
I thought if I were to go up
against Seong Beom...

102
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:34,810
in Pyramid Number, I might lose.

103
00:04:37,750 --> 00:04:39,480
(Pyramid Number)

104
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:43,320
You have selected Pyramid Number.

105
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:46,620
So I decided to play Pyramid Number
with Sung Joo.

106
00:04:47,690 --> 00:04:49,460
I hope Round Three ends up
being Card Chess.

107
00:04:50,830 --> 00:04:53,930
(Round 1: Pyramid Number)

108
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,270
YunB, you won second place
in the semifinal match.

109
00:04:56,430 --> 00:04:59,240
Go to the Voting Room. And select a game.

110
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:01,810
Is there a game you want to play?

111
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:03,880
Which one did you pick, Ji Hoo?

112
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:06,140
I picked Pyramid Number.

113
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:08,310
(The remaining options are
Card Chess and Choice Hold'em.)

114
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:10,520
Well, either one is fine.

115
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:11,580
- Either one is fine?
- Yes.

116
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:13,550
Do you want to play Choice Hold'em?

117
00:05:13,690 --> 00:05:15,750
- Sounds good.
- Good. Let's play that.

118
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:21,360
I felt confident going into any game.

119
00:05:22,090 --> 00:05:24,860
My only blind spot would be betting games.

120
00:05:24,860 --> 00:05:28,900
It might be because I haven't played
a lot of poker or betting games.

121
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:30,770
So I'm not good at those games.

122
00:05:30,970 --> 00:05:33,470
Anyway, to make it to the top,

123
00:05:33,670 --> 00:05:36,110
I should be able to perform well
with these games too.

124
00:05:42,650 --> 00:05:44,650
You have selected Choice Hold'em.

125
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:46,720
I shine the most when it comes to...

126
00:05:47,050 --> 00:05:49,190
mind games or social deduction games.

127
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:52,560
My strength is
reading my opponent's hand...

128
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:54,660
and anticipating their moves.

129
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:56,060
Mind games are my strong suit.

130
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,060
(He chose a game
he may have the upper hand in.)

131
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,730
The games for the rounds have been chosen.

132
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:06,370
(Round 1: Pyramid Number)

133
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:13,210
Round One of the final match
will begin now.

134
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:31,860
I love these.

135
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:38,000
I saw all my favorite things.
A blackboard, numbers,

136
00:06:38,140 --> 00:06:39,500
and math symbols.

137
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:42,110
I didn't know what the game
was going to be. But it looked like...

138
00:06:42,510 --> 00:06:43,710
I had to combine them to make a number.

139
00:06:44,110 --> 00:06:45,680
The moment I saw the square root symbol,
I knew I had it in the bag.

140
00:06:46,910 --> 00:06:49,650
Hey, it's been over 20 years
since I hadn't seen this symbol.

141
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:54,020
When I saw numbers and math symbols,
I knew I was at a disadvantage.

142
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:57,590
Even with my brain firing on all cylinders
like back when I took the CSAT,

143
00:06:57,590 --> 00:06:59,490
I would still lose to Ji Hoo.

144
00:06:59,590 --> 00:07:00,790
But I have to do this
with my current brain power?

145
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:05,560
It's been over ten years
since I last solved a math problem.

146
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:13,500
Hello.

147
00:07:14,110 --> 00:07:16,170
Welcome to Round One...

148
00:07:16,410 --> 00:07:19,410
of the final match of Bloody Game X.

149
00:07:20,810 --> 00:07:22,880
The winner of Round One...

150
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:25,180
will advance
to Round Three of the final match.

151
00:07:25,950 --> 00:07:28,220
The losing player will be eliminated
from the show...

152
00:07:28,750 --> 00:07:30,660
and must leave Bloody Game X.

153
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:34,860
Here's Round One of the final match.

154
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:37,500
Round One of the final match is...

155
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:42,170
Pyramid Number.

156
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:44,100
(Pyramid Number)

157
00:07:44,870 --> 00:07:48,110
In Pyramid Number,
players must use three given numbers...

158
00:07:48,470 --> 00:07:52,140
to reach the target number
in the pyramid before your opponent.

159
00:07:52,610 --> 00:07:55,750
Players will receive 14 number tiles...

160
00:07:56,250 --> 00:07:57,850
and 12 operation tiles.

161
00:07:58,450 --> 00:08:01,050
They will have a total of 26 tiles.

162
00:08:02,250 --> 00:08:04,490
The game consists of ten rounds.

163
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:08,130
At the beginning of the round,
three numbers for calculation...

164
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:12,230
and 14 target numbers arranged
in a pyramid form will be revealed.

165
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:17,540
Players must use up
all three given numbers...

166
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:21,270
to formulate an expression
that equals one of the target numbers.

167
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:25,080
There is no set number
on how many target numbers...

168
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:27,680
can be cleared in a round.

169
00:08:28,050 --> 00:08:31,180
Some rounds may offer
no valid expressions at all.

170
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:35,790
A player with a complete expression
can call out to provide an answer.

171
00:08:36,950 --> 00:08:38,590
The player who calls out to do so...

172
00:08:38,890 --> 00:08:42,690
must present an expression that
equals a target number in five seconds.

173
00:08:43,190 --> 00:08:45,630
The player will lose a point
with an incorrect answer.

174
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:47,300
When the player presents
a correct expression,

175
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:49,670
the opposing player has 30 seconds...

176
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:53,170
to present an expression that
equals a target number in a higher row.

177
00:08:54,110 --> 00:08:56,470
Presenting an incorrect expression
during this turn...

178
00:08:56,470 --> 00:08:57,880
won't result in a point penalty.

179
00:08:58,440 --> 00:09:00,440
If the opposing player presents
a correct expression...

180
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:02,710
that hits a target number in a higher row,

181
00:09:03,210 --> 00:09:06,120
the initial player gets 30 seconds
and a chance...

182
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:08,650
to reach a target number in a higher row.

183
00:09:09,190 --> 00:09:10,990
When a player hits a target number...

184
00:09:10,990 --> 00:09:13,820
in the highest row of the pyramid,

185
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:15,830
the round ends
as the player is awarded with points.

186
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:18,900
Points vary based on...

187
00:09:18,900 --> 00:09:22,530
the row level
of their final target number.

188
00:09:23,330 --> 00:09:26,600
When no one has called out
to present an expression,

189
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,870
players can declare
that the pyramid is unsolvable.

190
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:32,140
When a player declares it unsolvable,

191
00:09:32,210 --> 00:09:34,850
the opposing player receives one minute.

192
00:09:35,380 --> 00:09:38,720
If the player fails to reach
any target number during this minute,

193
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:41,620
the declaration for an unsolvable pyramid
is confirmed valid.

194
00:09:41,790 --> 00:09:44,690
The player with the declaration
receives five points.

195
00:09:45,820 --> 00:09:49,430
If the opposing player can present
a correct expression within a minute,

196
00:09:49,890 --> 00:09:53,200
the player with the declaration
loses three points.

197
00:09:53,530 --> 00:09:55,100
The player with the correct expression...

198
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:58,040
earns the point value
of that target number.

199
00:09:59,170 --> 00:10:00,740
After all ten rounds,

200
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:02,670
the player with more points...

201
00:10:02,870 --> 00:10:05,940
will be the winner
of Round One of the final match.

202
00:10:07,850 --> 00:10:10,310
Round One of the final match,

203
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:13,250
Pyramid Number, will begin shortly.

204
00:10:16,850 --> 00:10:18,490
It was just as I had expected.

205
00:10:18,890 --> 00:10:21,760
We were going to get 14 numbers.
And we had to combine numbers to hit them.

206
00:10:22,290 --> 00:10:23,460
My only concern is...

207
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:25,460
that I'm not quick on my feet.

208
00:10:25,830 --> 00:10:28,930
If we end up with easy ones
and it's all about volume,

209
00:10:29,470 --> 00:10:30,500
I might lose.

210
00:10:31,470 --> 00:10:34,970
As expected, we had to combine numbers
and operation symbols to make expressions.

211
00:10:34,970 --> 00:10:37,810
No matter how good anyone is,
people make mistakes.

212
00:10:37,810 --> 00:10:39,380
It's a fast-paced game.

213
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:41,910
If there was any shortcut,
I wanted to make good use of it.

214
00:10:41,910 --> 00:10:43,680
My evaluation of Ji Hoo is that...

215
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:45,150
he can be stubborn.

216
00:10:45,350 --> 00:10:48,920
And he knows too well that he's smart.

217
00:10:49,150 --> 00:10:51,790
When he's stuck, he'll be stubborn
and keep trying to find an answer.

218
00:10:51,790 --> 00:10:53,520
But I'll switch to another number.

219
00:10:53,790 --> 00:10:55,530
In that sense, I might be more flexible.

220
00:10:55,530 --> 00:10:57,600
I thought that was my only advantage.

221
00:10:58,460 --> 00:11:00,800
We will begin Round One now.

222
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:04,340
Here's the first problem.

223
00:11:14,850 --> 00:11:18,280
The given numbers for your expression
are 3, 5, and 8.

224
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:20,020
(They must form an expression
with 3, 5, and 8.)

225
00:11:22,390 --> 00:11:25,290
The goal of this game is
winning four points no matter what.

226
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:27,320
It doesn't matter
if I win 1, 2, or 3 points.

227
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:30,800
If the opposing player wins 4 points
within 30 seconds,

228
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,400
I'll lose all of my points.

229
00:11:33,230 --> 00:11:35,230
On the other hand,
if I win four points from the get-go,

230
00:11:35,230 --> 00:11:36,570
there's nothing my opponent can do.

231
00:11:36,630 --> 00:11:39,000
My winning strategy is
only going after four points.

232
00:11:39,340 --> 00:11:41,010
I won't even look at the other numbers
in the pyramid...

233
00:11:41,010 --> 00:11:42,670
except for two numbers in the top row.

234
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:46,010
(He checks the numbers on Row 4.)

235
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:47,680
We got 3, 5, and 8.

236
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:49,280
Then we had 15 and 20 on Row 4.

237
00:11:49,910 --> 00:11:51,280
I had to break down the numbers first.

238
00:11:52,450 --> 00:11:54,650
Three times five is fifteen.
Two squared times five is twenty.

239
00:11:54,650 --> 00:11:55,690
Both of them are multiples of five.

240
00:11:56,350 --> 00:11:58,520
It didn't work with 3 and 8.

241
00:11:59,290 --> 00:12:01,530
Squaring them didn't work.
Taking the square root didn't work either.

242
00:12:02,060 --> 00:12:03,960
Nothing worked.
I didn't know where to go from there.

243
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:08,530
I have an answer.

244
00:12:11,370 --> 00:12:12,400
Sixteen.

245
00:12:17,910 --> 00:12:18,940
That's correct.

246
00:12:18,940 --> 00:12:21,380
Sung Joo,
you've completed a number on Row One.

247
00:12:21,380 --> 00:12:24,250
(Sung Joo gets a target number on Row 1.)

248
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:25,820
Right before we started,

249
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:28,250
I wrote down numbers such as 13 and 15,

250
00:12:28,390 --> 00:12:29,820
squares, and cubes...

251
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:32,590
on my hand. Then I quickly
transferred them to the notebook.

252
00:12:32,590 --> 00:12:34,490
I played the game
with these numbers ready.

253
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:36,790
I would be able
to calculate numbers faster...

