505
00:26:09,770 --> 00:26:10,910
My answer is 154.

506
00:26:12,380 --> 00:26:13,410
Sung Joo,

507
00:26:14,640 --> 00:26:15,780
that's correct.

508
00:26:19,650 --> 00:26:21,150
He must have thought...

509
00:26:21,150 --> 00:26:23,450
that I found these expressions difficult.

510
00:26:23,590 --> 00:26:26,220
I'm guessing he called it out...

511
00:26:26,220 --> 00:26:28,390
because he strongly believed
I'd never get it before he did.

512
00:26:29,190 --> 00:26:30,430
But he made 154.

513
00:26:31,260 --> 00:26:34,000
I realized he could do that much
in his head.

514
00:26:34,260 --> 00:26:37,830
Ji Hoo, you failed to correctly declare,
"Unsolvable," and lost three points.

515
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:40,470
Sung Joo gets one point.

516
00:26:40,940 --> 00:26:43,310
(There are two problems left.)

517
00:26:44,110 --> 00:26:46,210
We will begin Round Nine now.

518
00:26:46,480 --> 00:26:47,740
Here's the problem.

519
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:54,750
Unsolvable.

520
00:26:54,750 --> 00:26:56,150
(Sung Joo calls out, "Unsolvable.")

521
00:26:56,420 --> 00:26:57,690
I declared it right away.

522
00:26:58,120 --> 00:26:59,920
I didn't have a choice at the time.

523
00:27:00,190 --> 00:27:01,560
What would be the point
of getting one point?

524
00:27:01,560 --> 00:27:02,960
All I could do with that was tell my mom.

525
00:27:04,390 --> 00:27:08,060
Ji Hoo, you have one minute
to try to get the answer.

526
00:27:09,970 --> 00:27:11,300
The numbers didn't matter.

527
00:27:11,300 --> 00:27:14,440
I knew I'd lose if I got one point.

528
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:15,510
I needed five points.

529
00:27:16,510 --> 00:27:19,240
That was the only way to win
by getting five points at once.

530
00:27:22,080 --> 00:27:24,780
(Making noises)

531
00:27:28,250 --> 00:27:32,160
(He bustles and distracts him.)

532
00:27:36,590 --> 00:27:40,000
(Like a library nuisance)

533
00:27:41,060 --> 00:27:42,730
Your time is up.

534
00:27:42,730 --> 00:27:44,930
(His 1 minute is up.)

535
00:27:45,540 --> 00:27:49,110
Sung Joo, you successfully declared,
"Unsolvable," and earned five points.

536
00:27:50,310 --> 00:27:51,780
I thought I'd be fine at that rate.

537
00:27:51,780 --> 00:27:54,180
(Sung Joo turns it around
and he is 3 points ahead.)

538
00:27:54,180 --> 00:27:56,210
We will begin Round Ten now.

539
00:27:56,980 --> 00:27:58,310
Here's the problem.

540
00:27:58,620 --> 00:28:02,150
The given numbers for your expression
are 6, 13, and 15.

541
00:28:03,850 --> 00:28:04,890
Unsolvable.

542
00:28:05,590 --> 00:28:07,790
Ji Hoo has called out, "Unsolvable."

543
00:28:12,460 --> 00:28:15,070
I was certain he'd call out, "Unsolvable,"

544
00:28:15,070 --> 00:28:16,130
but he didn't.

545
00:28:16,330 --> 00:28:19,270
I was lucky enough to call it out first.

546
00:28:19,270 --> 00:28:22,810
Sung Joo, you have one minute
to try to get the answer.

547
00:28:25,510 --> 00:28:31,750
(If he gets the answer,
he advances to Round 3.)

548
00:28:34,420 --> 00:28:36,120
The easiest ones were on the first row,

549
00:28:36,120 --> 00:28:38,250
so I tried to calculate those.

550
00:28:38,620 --> 00:28:41,190
Six, four, seven, seventy, hundred...

551
00:28:42,090 --> 00:28:44,090
But nothing was obvious on the first row.

552
00:28:46,860 --> 00:28:49,300
I was looking at the problem with him,
and it was so tricky.

553
00:28:49,670 --> 00:28:51,330
No multiples of 13 and 15 worked.

554
00:28:52,070 --> 00:28:54,300
The easiest one was ten,
the smallest number.

555
00:28:54,870 --> 00:28:57,070
I did 13 minus the square root
of 15 minus 6, and I got it.

556
00:28:58,610 --> 00:29:00,510
I was praying he'd never get it.

557
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:27,940
I was like, "Hold on."

558
00:29:29,770 --> 00:29:31,310
"Was declaring 'unsolvable' a bad idea?"

559
00:29:38,620 --> 00:29:41,120
Round One of the final match has ended.

560
00:29:41,120 --> 00:29:42,450
(Pyramid Number ends.)

561
00:29:44,820 --> 00:29:47,790
Here's the result
of Round One of the final match.

562
00:29:50,790 --> 00:29:53,130
The winner
of Round One of the final match is...

563
00:29:59,240 --> 00:30:00,870
Kang Ji Hoo.

564
00:30:00,870 --> 00:30:02,570
(Ji Hoo wins Round 1 of the final match.)

565
00:30:12,780 --> 00:30:15,320
I added, subtracted, and multiplied...

566
00:30:16,020 --> 00:30:18,790
a few combinations,
and none of them worked.

567
00:30:18,790 --> 00:30:23,590
(He focused on the 1st row,
but none of them was solvable.)

568
00:30:23,790 --> 00:30:26,430
Even if I were about to lose
or I wasn't sure,

569
00:30:26,430 --> 00:30:29,800
I just wanted to show people
that I was trying.

570
00:30:29,800 --> 00:30:31,230
Doing my best was all I could do.

571
00:30:32,870 --> 00:30:34,370
Your time is up.

572
00:30:35,100 --> 00:30:37,270
Ji Hoo, you successfully declared,
"Unsolvable,"

573
00:30:37,270 --> 00:30:38,680
and earned five points.

574
00:30:39,540 --> 00:30:41,310
Round Ten has ended.

575
00:30:41,310 --> 00:30:42,880
(The final score is 10 to 8.)

576
00:30:42,880 --> 00:30:46,020
If Ji Hoo wins the next game as well,

577
00:30:46,480 --> 00:30:49,490
he becomes the final winner
of Bloody Game X.

578
00:30:50,650 --> 00:30:53,620
Sung Joo, please leave immediately.

579
00:30:56,730 --> 00:30:57,730
Great work.

580
00:31:00,900 --> 00:31:02,370
I don't feel bad for losing.

581
00:31:03,500 --> 00:31:05,400
It's not embarrassing for me...

582
00:31:05,970 --> 00:31:07,500
to lose to Ji Hoo.

583
00:31:07,600 --> 00:31:09,470
I could happily congratulate him.

584
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:13,980
I think I could survive longer
than last time for just one reason.

585
00:31:13,980 --> 00:31:15,040
Back then,

586
00:31:15,810 --> 00:31:17,880
I felt like I could win
only if I deserved to win...

587
00:31:17,880 --> 00:31:20,150
and I thought I should take responsibility
if I didn't deserve it.

588
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:21,990
I was obsessed with that thought.

589
00:31:23,220 --> 00:31:24,590
Do you want to stay for more games?

590
00:31:24,750 --> 00:31:25,790
Do you want to stay for more games?

591
00:31:25,790 --> 00:31:27,020
I want to go.

592
00:31:27,290 --> 00:31:28,290
Why?

593
00:31:28,290 --> 00:31:30,460
I feel the limit of my brain.

594
00:31:31,360 --> 00:31:32,960
- Are you serious?
- Yes.

595
00:31:32,960 --> 00:31:37,800
(He tried to test his worth in Season 2.)

596
00:31:38,470 --> 00:31:40,770
And 2 or 3 years have passed.

597
00:31:41,800 --> 00:31:43,370
I came back a little more shameless.

598
00:31:44,570 --> 00:31:47,210
I tried to survive,
even if it meant acting like a parasite.

599
00:31:47,340 --> 00:31:50,510
And if I'm kicked out for being too bad...

600
00:31:50,510 --> 00:31:51,680
or being hated by others,

601
00:31:51,680 --> 00:31:53,450
I'll think about it then.

602
00:31:53,720 --> 00:31:55,420
Why would I willingly leave before that?

603
00:31:55,920 --> 00:31:57,220
That was my mindset.

604
00:31:57,220 --> 00:31:58,860
I think that made all the difference.

605
00:31:58,960 --> 00:32:01,720
There are many factors
that help you survive...

606
00:32:02,160 --> 00:32:03,360
through all those stages.

607
00:32:03,360 --> 00:32:04,760
It's not just your IQ...

608
00:32:04,760 --> 00:32:06,460
or EQ.

609
00:32:06,930 --> 00:32:08,460
Even when you feel like the underdog,

610
00:32:09,300 --> 00:32:11,570
you'll see an opening
that will help you survive...

611
00:32:11,570 --> 00:32:13,240
if you keep your eyes peeled.

612
00:32:13,470 --> 00:32:15,470
I want people to realize that.

613
00:32:16,370 --> 00:32:19,580
I'm glad I could gain the hope of winning.

614
00:32:20,880 --> 00:32:23,410
Next time, I'll hone my skills so much...

615
00:32:23,750 --> 00:32:26,350
that I won't even need to be shameless...

616
00:32:26,350 --> 00:32:27,820
to win.

617
00:32:29,790 --> 00:32:30,950
It was fun.

618
00:32:31,350 --> 00:32:33,590
(Round 1, Pyramid Number)

619
00:32:33,590 --> 00:32:34,820
(Round 3, Card Chess, Kang Ji Hoo)

620
00:32:34,820 --> 00:32:37,030
(Round 2, Choice Hold'em,
YunB versus Heo Seong Beom)

621
00:32:37,560 --> 00:32:41,500
Round Two of the final match
will begin now.

622
00:32:56,550 --> 00:32:58,550
Rather than saying,
"I'm confident that I'll win,"

623
00:32:58,550 --> 00:33:00,320
I'd say, "I can't see myself losing."

624
00:33:01,020 --> 00:33:02,850
He's built for survival.

625
00:33:02,920 --> 00:33:06,360
He looked like a guy who cared
more about results than the process.

626
00:33:06,490 --> 00:33:07,890
Spending time with him,

627
00:33:07,890 --> 00:33:09,230
I thought,
"Does he want to go that far..."

628
00:33:09,560 --> 00:33:10,730
"to survive?"

629
00:33:11,590 --> 00:33:13,760
Whether he played well or not,

630
00:33:13,760 --> 00:33:15,630
he was fine if he survived.

631
00:33:16,470 --> 00:33:19,400
He always loved to survive
without having to earn it,

632
00:33:19,400 --> 00:33:22,610
so I used to look at him and think,
"I wonder how long that will last."

633
00:33:23,310 --> 00:33:24,940
To be honest,

634
00:33:24,940 --> 00:33:27,210
Seong Beom is too by-the-book.

635
00:33:27,610 --> 00:33:30,010
I have to beat him to prove...

636
00:33:30,180 --> 00:33:31,910
that a wild card, unorthodox,

637
00:33:32,750 --> 00:33:35,950
survivalist player like me can also win...

638
00:33:35,950 --> 00:33:38,320
in this world of survival.

639
00:33:38,320 --> 00:33:42,460
I need to beat a textbook perfectionist,
elite, and handsome greedy player...

640
00:33:42,460 --> 00:33:44,230
to complete this story.

641
00:33:48,660 --> 00:33:50,070
Hello, everyone.

642
00:33:50,170 --> 00:33:52,440
Welcome to Round Two...

643
00:33:52,500 --> 00:33:55,840
of the final match of Bloody Game X.

644
00:33:56,040 --> 00:33:58,170
The winner of Round Two...

645
00:33:58,470 --> 00:34:01,040
will advance
to Round Three of the final match.

646
00:34:01,180 --> 00:34:03,850
The losing player will be eliminated
from the show...

647
00:34:03,850 --> 00:34:06,220
and must leave Bloody Game X.

648
00:34:06,520 --> 00:34:09,520
Here's Round Two of the final match.

649
00:34:09,920 --> 00:34:12,060
Round Two of the final match is...

650
00:34:12,460 --> 00:34:13,820
(Choice Hold'em)

651
00:34:13,820 --> 00:34:16,590
Choice Hold'em.

652
00:34:17,530 --> 00:34:20,430
Choice Hold'em is a card game...

653
00:34:20,430 --> 00:34:22,400
where players combine
three community cards...

654
00:34:22,470 --> 00:34:24,430
and two hole cards to build...

655
00:34:24,430 --> 00:34:26,500
the strongest possible hand
and place their bets.

656
00:34:26,770 --> 00:34:31,940
Before the game starts,
both players receive 20 betting chips.

657
00:34:32,710 --> 00:34:34,280
When a round begins,

658
00:34:34,280 --> 00:34:38,050
players must make a blind bet of one chip,

659
00:34:38,410 --> 00:34:42,850
which increases by 1 chip every 10 rounds.

660
00:34:43,750 --> 00:34:47,960
The game uses a deck of 20 cards,
consisting of 4 sets of numbers...

661
00:34:48,020 --> 00:34:50,560
from 1 to 5.

662
00:34:51,130 --> 00:34:56,230
First, each player receives one hole card,

663
00:34:56,430 --> 00:35:00,340
and three community cards are dealt
face-up in the center of the table.

664
00:35:00,840 --> 00:35:04,470
Then, the 1st player begins
the 1st round of betting,

665
00:35:04,770 --> 00:35:08,810
with the starting role
alternating every round.

666
00:35:09,650 --> 00:35:14,020
On their turn, a player can choose
1 of 3 actions.

667
00:35:14,650 --> 00:35:16,590
First, call.

668
00:35:16,990 --> 00:35:20,220
You may bet the same number of chips
as the opponent.

669
00:35:20,860 --> 00:35:23,030
Second, raise.

670
00:35:23,290 --> 00:35:26,400
You may bet more chips than the opponent.

671
00:35:26,860 --> 00:35:29,000
Third, fold.

672
00:35:29,300 --> 00:35:31,370
You may forfeit the round,

673
00:35:31,700 --> 00:35:34,800
in which case the cards remain hidden...

674
00:35:34,900 --> 00:35:37,770
and the opponent takes
all chips in the pot.

675
00:35:39,080 --> 00:35:41,280
Once the first betting round ends...

676
00:35:41,280 --> 00:35:42,910
with both players matching bets,

677
00:35:43,180 --> 00:35:45,880
two cards are dealt to the first player.

678
00:35:46,850 --> 00:35:49,150
After checking them,

679
00:35:49,150 --> 00:35:50,720
the first player must place one face-up...

680
00:35:50,720 --> 00:35:52,890
and one face-down.

681
00:35:53,290 --> 00:35:56,990
The 2nd player chooses
1 of the 2 cards to take,

682
00:35:57,030 --> 00:36:00,160
and the first player takes
the remaining one.

683
00:36:01,100 --> 00:36:02,500
Once the cards are selected,

684
00:36:02,500 --> 00:36:07,400
the 2nd round of betting begins
in the same manner as the 1st.

685
00:36:08,300 --> 00:36:10,010
When the second bet ends,

686
00:36:10,010 --> 00:36:12,140
both players reveal their hole cards,

687
00:36:12,510 --> 00:36:15,680
and the player
who forms the stronger hand...

688
00:36:15,680 --> 00:36:18,350
using their 2 hole cards
and the 3 community cards...

689
00:36:18,350 --> 00:36:21,380
takes all the chips in the pot.

690
00:36:21,950 --> 00:36:24,550
The hand rankings are as follows.

691
00:36:25,250 --> 00:36:27,590
The lowest is one pair,

692
00:36:27,590 --> 00:36:29,330
two cards of the same number.

693
00:36:30,130 --> 00:36:31,860
Next is two pair,

694
00:36:31,860 --> 00:36:34,260
two sets of matching numbers.

695
00:36:35,060 --> 00:36:36,630
Next is three of a kind,

696
00:36:36,630 --> 00:36:38,670
three cards of the same number.

697
00:36:39,400 --> 00:36:41,040
Next is a straight,

698
00:36:41,040 --> 00:36:46,080
a sequence of 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5.

699
00:36:46,740 --> 00:36:48,440
Next is a full house,

700
00:36:48,440 --> 00:36:51,210
a set of three matching numbers
and a pair of matching numbers.

701
00:36:51,580 --> 00:36:53,120
Next is four of a kind,

702
00:36:53,120 --> 00:36:54,950
four cards of the same number.

703
00:36:55,690 --> 00:36:57,120
If players have the same hand rank,

704
00:36:57,120 --> 00:36:59,760
the hand with the higher number wins.

705
00:37:00,190 --> 00:37:02,160
If the hand numbers are also identical,

706
00:37:02,260 --> 00:37:04,590
the player holding...

707
00:37:04,590 --> 00:37:07,360
the higher unused hole card wins.

708
00:37:08,200 --> 00:37:10,570
If even the unused hole cards
are identical,

709
00:37:10,570 --> 00:37:13,170
the chips remain in the pot...

710
00:37:13,170 --> 00:37:15,040
and the game moves to the next round.

711
00:37:15,370 --> 00:37:17,870
In this situation,
we will not switch the first player...

712
00:37:17,940 --> 00:37:20,280
or take additional bets.

713
00:37:21,110 --> 00:37:24,650
If a player lacks enough chips
to pay the basic bet,

714
00:37:24,650 --> 00:37:27,850
the game ends immediately
with that player's defeat.

715
00:37:28,990 --> 00:37:32,590
Choice Hold'em will begin shortly.

716
00:37:35,420 --> 00:37:36,630
It's the same as poker.

717
00:37:36,630 --> 00:37:37,660
Is it?

718
00:37:37,660 --> 00:37:39,260
- Yes, it's the same rule.
- I've never played poker.

719
00:37:39,260 --> 00:37:40,630
It's the same.

720
00:37:41,400 --> 00:37:44,300
I had never played poker in my life.

721
00:37:44,300 --> 00:37:45,900
YunB was my opponent,

722
00:37:46,070 --> 00:37:48,670
and he must have played poker
more than me.

723
00:37:48,670 --> 00:37:50,910
But I have better abilities...

724
00:37:50,910 --> 00:37:52,610
of reading the game...

725
00:37:52,610 --> 00:37:55,910
and coming up with strategies.

726
00:37:55,910 --> 00:37:58,010
So, I'll aim to keep up
with his experience...

727
00:37:58,010 --> 00:38:01,550
as I play the game.

728
00:38:02,390 --> 00:38:04,950
I was relieved...

729
00:38:04,950 --> 00:38:07,060
that the rules were simpler than expected.

730
00:38:07,060 --> 00:38:10,230
But the biggest mystery was...

731
00:38:10,260 --> 00:38:12,060
why the name "Choice?"

732
00:38:12,060 --> 00:38:13,600
I'm supposed to pick...

733
00:38:13,600 --> 00:38:15,030
between an open card...

734
00:38:15,030 --> 00:38:16,370
and a closed card.

735
00:38:16,370 --> 00:38:19,470
The winner may be determined...

736
00:38:19,470 --> 00:38:22,040
based on which card you place face-up.

737
00:38:22,970 --> 00:38:24,570
Round Two of the final match,

738
00:38:24,840 --> 00:38:27,510
Choice Hold'em will begin now.

739
00:38:29,250 --> 00:38:31,610
YunB, who ranked higher in the semifinals,

740
00:38:31,610 --> 00:38:33,380
will decide who goes first.

741
00:38:34,620 --> 00:38:37,820
YunB, would you like to go 1st or 2nd?

742
00:38:38,490 --> 00:38:39,990
I'll go first.

743
00:38:40,790 --> 00:38:42,490
I chose to go first...

744
00:38:43,060 --> 00:38:46,300
because my priority was
to see how he would respond.

745
00:38:47,260 --> 00:38:49,070
I can get familiar with the game...

746
00:38:49,070 --> 00:38:52,130
and see which card he chooses...

747
00:38:52,570 --> 00:38:55,040
earlier than him.

748
00:38:55,040 --> 00:38:56,340
That's why.

749
00:38:56,710 --> 00:39:00,040
The starting role will alternate
every round.

750
00:39:01,880 --> 00:39:04,410
Round One will begin now.

751
00:39:04,410 --> 00:39:10,120
(Round 1, YunB: 20, Heo Seong Beom: 20)

752
00:39:17,660 --> 00:39:22,730
(One hole card is dealt each.)

753
00:39:23,170 --> 00:39:25,200
(YunB's hole card: 5)

754
00:39:25,200 --> 00:39:27,870
Five was a pretty high number,

755
00:39:27,870 --> 00:39:29,940
so I was relieved.

756
00:39:29,940 --> 00:39:31,210
It wasn't the worst.

757
00:39:31,310 --> 00:39:32,740
Five is better than one.

758
00:39:34,610 --> 00:39:36,510
(Heo Seong Beom's hole card)

759
00:39:36,510 --> 00:39:39,520
I wanted to check his playing style.

760
00:39:39,620 --> 00:39:41,680
I was going to sit back
and keep an eye on him.

761
00:39:43,250 --> 00:39:46,090
Please place your base bet of one chip.

762
00:39:46,460 --> 00:39:49,990
(The base bet is 1 chip until Round 10.)

763
00:39:50,030 --> 00:39:52,130
Here are the community cards.

764
00:39:52,130 --> 00:39:58,200
(Community card: 3, 1, 3)

765
00:39:58,200 --> 00:40:00,770
We will proceed with the first bet.

766
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:03,970
YunB, place your bet.

767
00:40:07,540 --> 00:40:09,980
You have bet two chips.

768
00:40:10,980 --> 00:40:12,920
Seong Beom, place your bet.

769
00:40:12,920 --> 00:40:15,680
To call, you must bet two chips.

770
00:40:18,920 --> 00:40:22,790
When I play, I normally wait
for their reactions first,

771
00:40:22,790 --> 00:40:25,060
even if I have nothing.

772
00:40:25,060 --> 00:40:27,500
You know,
to figure out how he usually plays...

773
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:30,330
and what habits he has...

774
00:40:30,330 --> 00:40:33,170
when thinking hard.

775
00:40:33,670 --> 00:40:35,170
I acted like I wasn't,

776
00:40:35,170 --> 00:40:37,140
but I kept observing him.

777
00:40:45,750 --> 00:40:47,480
You have called.

778
00:40:47,480 --> 00:40:49,350
You have bet a total of two chips.

779
00:40:50,050 --> 00:40:52,920
(1st bet: 6 chips in total)

780
00:40:52,990 --> 00:40:56,060
The 1st player gets 2 cards.

781
00:40:59,400 --> 00:41:00,400
(Choice card: 5, 5)

782
00:41:00,400 --> 00:41:01,760
They were 5 and 5.

783
00:41:01,760 --> 00:41:05,430
I was given such good choices.

784
00:41:05,600 --> 00:41:08,900
I already had two pairs.

785
00:41:09,810 --> 00:41:11,910
Please place one card face up...

786
00:41:11,910 --> 00:41:13,880
and one card face down.

787
00:41:16,680 --> 00:41:19,620
(Choice card: 5)

788
00:41:20,280 --> 00:41:23,020
Seong Beom, please choose a card.

789
00:41:23,050 --> 00:41:25,650
You have chosen the card facing down.

790
00:41:28,590 --> 00:41:30,890
YunB, please take the card facing up.

791
00:41:33,360 --> 00:41:35,700
We will proceed with the second bet.

792
00:41:35,730 --> 00:41:37,430
YunB, place your bet.

793
00:41:39,200 --> 00:41:41,670
You have bet three chips.

794
00:41:42,240 --> 00:41:45,010
Obviously, I raised.

795
00:41:45,010 --> 00:41:46,410
I had two pairs,

796
00:41:46,410 --> 00:41:48,580
so unless he had three cards
of the same number,

797
00:41:48,580 --> 00:41:51,680
I could easily win.

798
00:41:52,350 --> 00:41:54,320
Seong Beom, place your bet.

799
00:41:54,580 --> 00:41:57,220
To call, you must bet
three additional chips.

800
00:41:58,450 --> 00:42:04,390
(If his hole card is 3,
he wins with a triple of 3s.)

801
00:42:08,960 --> 00:42:10,830
You have called.

802
00:42:10,830 --> 00:42:12,670
You have bet a total of three chips.

803
00:42:12,670 --> 00:42:14,840
(It's a big pot of 12 chips
from the 1st round.)

804
00:42:15,200 --> 00:42:18,310
And he called.

805
00:42:18,440 --> 00:42:19,680
That meant...

806
00:42:19,810 --> 00:42:21,180
he had at least a pair.

807
00:42:21,580 --> 00:42:24,980
(Who will get a head start in Round 1?)

808
00:42:25,650 --> 00:42:27,980
The hands will now be revealed.

809
00:42:28,720 --> 00:42:30,850
Seong Beom, please reveal your hand.

810
00:42:35,120 --> 00:42:36,260
(2 pair, 3s and 1s)

811
00:42:36,260 --> 00:42:38,830
Seong Beom, 2 pair, 3s and 1s.

812
00:42:40,760 --> 00:42:43,100
I didn't think my hand was strong.

813
00:42:43,100 --> 00:42:45,870
But I wanted to see his hand,
even if it meant spending my chips.

814
00:42:46,100 --> 00:42:49,610
I thought it was important to call
and check his cards...

815
00:42:49,610 --> 00:42:52,010
so that I could take the advantage...

816
00:42:52,010 --> 00:42:55,240
in the latter part of the game.

817
00:42:55,640 --> 00:42:58,150
YunB, 2 pair, 5s and 3s.

818
00:42:59,180 --> 00:43:01,580
YunB has won Round One.

819
00:43:02,450 --> 00:43:03,550
I was exhilarated.

820
00:43:03,550 --> 00:43:05,050
I was off to a smooth start.

821
00:43:05,190 --> 00:43:06,920
In poker,

822
00:43:06,920 --> 00:43:09,120
getting early momentum...

823
00:43:09,390 --> 00:43:12,230
gives you control...

824
00:43:12,230 --> 00:43:14,130
over the whole flow of the game,

825
00:43:14,130 --> 00:43:15,970
so I was satisfied with the result.

826
00:43:16,430 --> 00:43:18,130
We will begin Round Two now.

827
00:43:18,130 --> 00:43:19,230
(Round 2, YunB: 25, Heo Seong Beom: 13)

828
00:43:19,340 --> 00:43:21,500
(Heo Seong Beom's hole card: 5)

829
00:43:22,570 --> 00:43:25,440
(YunB's hole card)

830
00:43:25,510 --> 00:43:27,640
Here are the community cards.

831
00:43:28,980 --> 00:43:33,050
(Community card: 3, 5, 2)

832
00:43:33,120 --> 00:43:35,120
We will proceed with the first bet.

833
00:43:35,320 --> 00:43:37,390
Heo Seong Beom, place your bet.

834
00:43:37,920 --> 00:43:39,820
If there's literally one sentence...

835
00:43:39,820 --> 00:43:42,490
You Hyun told me about poker,

836
00:43:42,660 --> 00:43:44,730
it's that betting consistently is good.

837
00:43:44,730 --> 00:43:46,960
I heard that from him.

838
00:43:47,100 --> 00:43:48,830
"Should I be consistent in my bets?"

839
00:43:48,830 --> 00:43:51,300
And I bet one chip.

840
00:43:52,030 --> 00:43:54,570
You have bet one chip.

841
00:43:55,170 --> 00:43:56,770
YunB has called.

842
00:43:56,770 --> 00:43:58,470
You have bet one chip.

843
00:43:59,210 --> 00:44:01,610
Judging from the one chip,

844
00:44:01,680 --> 00:44:03,010
it's got to be a snap call.

845
00:44:03,010 --> 00:44:06,320
I thought it was worth paying...

846
00:44:06,320 --> 00:44:09,420
to see the next cards
and collect information.

847
00:44:09,920 --> 00:44:12,920
The 1st player gets 2 cards.

848
00:44:14,490 --> 00:44:20,060
(Choice card: 3, 2)

849
00:44:20,060 --> 00:44:21,860
Please place one card face up...

850
00:44:21,860 --> 00:44:23,870
and one card face down.

851
00:44:27,670 --> 00:44:29,870
(Face-up card, 3)

852
00:44:31,140 --> 00:44:34,210
As soon as I saw it, I thought...

853
00:44:34,610 --> 00:44:38,310
There's already three on the board.

854
00:44:38,580 --> 00:44:40,780
I think Seong Beom showed me the card...

855
00:44:40,780 --> 00:44:42,580
which he doesn't need.

856
00:44:42,580 --> 00:44:43,790
So I chose the card...

857
00:44:43,790 --> 00:44:45,590
he wanted to hide...

858
00:44:45,590 --> 00:44:48,420
instead of what he showed me.

859
00:44:49,190 --> 00:44:51,730
You have chosen the card facing down.

860
00:44:51,730 --> 00:44:53,000
(Round 2, YunB: 24, Heo Seong Beom: 12)

861
00:44:53,000 --> 00:44:55,030
We will proceed with the second bet.

862
00:44:55,660 --> 00:44:57,430
Heo Seong Beom, place your bet.

863
00:45:00,500 --> 00:45:03,140
You have bet three chips.

864
00:45:03,610 --> 00:45:05,110
It was a bait.

865
00:45:05,140 --> 00:45:07,680
If I raise the bet in this situation,

866
00:45:07,680 --> 00:45:10,050
what will he do? I should check it.

867
00:45:11,280 --> 00:45:12,450
(YunB has called to 3 chips.)

868
00:45:12,450 --> 00:45:14,120
YunB has called.

869
00:45:14,120 --> 00:45:15,750
You have bet three chips.

870
00:45:16,420 --> 00:45:18,050
All players have placed their bets.

871
00:45:18,320 --> 00:45:20,460
The hands will now be revealed.

872
00:45:21,290 --> 00:45:23,330
YunB, please reveal your hand.

873
00:45:25,430 --> 00:45:30,670
(YunB, a triple, 2s)

874
00:45:30,670 --> 00:45:32,670
YunB, a triple, 2s.

875
00:45:32,670 --> 00:45:34,370
(YunB, a triple, 2s)

876
00:45:34,370 --> 00:45:36,670
I did it.

877
00:45:37,870 --> 00:45:39,510
(Humming)

878
00:45:39,510 --> 00:45:40,980
This is why poker is fun.

879
00:45:44,250 --> 00:45:46,320
Heo Seong Beom, please reveal your hand.

880
00:45:48,950 --> 00:45:51,320
Heo Seong Beom, 2 pair, 5s and 3s.

881
00:45:51,820 --> 00:45:54,120
YunB has won Round Two.

882
00:45:54,120 --> 00:45:55,320
(YunB has won Round 2.)

883
00:45:55,320 --> 00:45:58,760
In this game, I gained the upper hand.

884
00:46:00,900 --> 00:46:03,470
We will begin Round Three now.

885
00:46:04,100 --> 00:46:05,230
Fold.

886
00:46:05,270 --> 00:46:07,270
Heo Seong Beom. You have folded.

887
00:46:08,870 --> 00:46:10,670
YunB. You have folded.

888
00:46:11,210 --> 00:46:13,280
We will begin Round Five now.

889
00:46:15,580 --> 00:46:17,910
(YunB's hole card: 3)

890
00:46:17,910 --> 00:46:19,920
Here are the community cards.

891
00:46:19,920 --> 00:46:23,990
(Community card: 1, 5, 4)

892
00:46:23,990 --> 00:46:25,750
You need to aim for a straight.

893
00:46:26,190 --> 00:46:29,160
The hand is perfect for a straight.

894
00:46:29,930 --> 00:46:31,790
(YunB can form a straight if he gets 2.)

895
00:46:31,790 --> 00:46:33,830
We will proceed with the first bet.

896
00:46:35,130 --> 00:46:37,370
YunB, you have bet two chips.

897
00:46:38,930 --> 00:46:40,470
Heo Seong Beom has called.

898
00:46:40,470 --> 00:46:42,340
You have bet two chips.

899
00:46:42,500 --> 00:46:45,540
The 1st player gets 2 cards.

900
00:46:49,310 --> 00:46:52,780
(Both are 4.)

901
00:46:52,780 --> 00:46:54,520
Please place one card face up...

902
00:46:54,520 --> 00:46:56,590
and one card face down.

903
00:46:59,090 --> 00:47:01,760
Heo Seong Beom.
You have chosen the card facing down.

904
00:47:02,990 --> 00:47:04,890
We will proceed with the second bet.

905
00:47:05,560 --> 00:47:07,330
YunB, place your bet.

906
00:47:08,530 --> 00:47:11,470
It's impossible to get a straight...

907
00:47:11,900 --> 00:47:14,370
because a pair of four has formed.

908
00:47:17,410 --> 00:47:19,980
YunB has bet five chips.

909
00:47:19,980 --> 00:47:21,910
(YunB has bet 5 chips.)

910
00:47:21,940 --> 00:47:23,850
Heo Seong Beom, place your bet.

911
00:47:24,080 --> 00:47:30,850
(To call, he needs to bet
all the chips he has.)

912
00:47:30,890 --> 00:47:34,020
Actually, there was no straight option,

913
00:47:34,020 --> 00:47:35,820
so my bet was a bluff.

914
00:47:35,820 --> 00:47:37,790
What I wanted to show here was...

915
00:47:37,960 --> 00:47:40,560
for Seong Beom to take the bluff and fold.

916
00:47:40,560 --> 00:47:42,660
I wanted him to fold.

917
00:47:49,400 --> 00:47:51,470
When I calculated the probability,

918
00:47:51,470 --> 00:47:53,980
since the four-card was taken by him,

919
00:47:54,010 --> 00:47:55,440
it was...

920
00:47:55,980 --> 00:47:57,280
a draw at best.

921
00:47:57,850 --> 00:47:59,850
Isn't it worth betting?

922
00:48:09,190 --> 00:48:10,790
(Heo Seong Beom has called to go all in.)

923
00:48:10,790 --> 00:48:12,830
Heo Seong Beom, you have gone all in.

924
00:48:13,960 --> 00:48:15,960
Does he have a triple of four?

925
00:48:16,330 --> 00:48:18,770
That must be the only way.

926
00:48:18,900 --> 00:48:21,040
It's either a 2 pair or 3 of a kind.

927
00:48:21,140 --> 00:48:23,240
The hands will now be revealed.

928
00:48:23,740 --> 00:48:26,010
Heo Seong Beom, please reveal your hand.

929
00:48:26,940 --> 00:48:31,210
(Heo Seong Beom, 1 pair, 4)

930
00:48:31,480 --> 00:48:34,480
(Same combination
with the same hole cards)

931
00:48:34,550 --> 00:48:38,120
Since both players have the same hand
and hole cards,

932
00:48:38,320 --> 00:48:40,990
the betting chips carry over
to the next round.

933
00:48:42,190 --> 00:48:44,090
I saw that and thought,

934
00:48:44,090 --> 00:48:45,290
"What's wrong with this guy?"

935
00:48:45,830 --> 00:48:49,000
Why did he join me in the bet?

936
00:48:49,160 --> 00:48:51,470
Calling for five chips...

937
00:48:51,470 --> 00:48:54,800
with such a poor hand as a pair of four...

938
00:48:54,970 --> 00:48:56,240
He called for it...

939
00:48:56,240 --> 00:48:59,270
when the risk was huge for himself.

940
00:48:59,270 --> 00:49:01,980
He either doesn't understand the game
or has a shallow understanding.

941
00:49:01,980 --> 00:49:03,550
It is quite risky, yes.

942
00:49:03,550 --> 00:49:05,580
If I go all in,

943
00:49:05,580 --> 00:49:07,450
I'll run out of chips.

944
00:49:07,450 --> 00:49:10,420
But I made a bold choice in that moment.

945
00:49:10,890 --> 00:49:13,560
(Seong Beom's fate will be decided
in the next round.)

946
00:49:13,560 --> 00:49:15,390
We will begin Round Six now.

947
00:49:17,960 --> 00:49:20,160
(The carryover round continues
with the same player going first.)

948
00:49:20,160 --> 00:49:21,630
(YunB's hole card: 4)

949
00:49:22,960 --> 00:49:24,500
(Heo Seong Beom's hole card: 2)

950
00:49:26,370 --> 00:49:28,300
Here are the community cards.

951
00:49:29,970 --> 00:49:33,480
(Community card: 3, 3, 1)

952
00:49:33,480 --> 00:49:34,610
I thought I was doomed.

953
00:49:34,610 --> 00:49:35,740
Darn it.

954
00:49:35,740 --> 00:49:37,880
When I got the first card, I thought,
"This looks bad."

955
00:49:38,580 --> 00:49:41,580
The 1st player gets 2 cards.

956
00:49:45,750 --> 00:49:47,490
This is...

957
00:49:47,690 --> 00:49:50,060
impossible.

958
00:49:52,260 --> 00:49:55,500
(The choice card is 3,
which he can make a 3 of a kind.)

959
00:49:55,500 --> 00:49:56,730
Please place one card face up...

960
00:49:56,730 --> 00:49:58,630
and one card face down.

961
00:50:01,740 --> 00:50:03,610
This is a trick of fate.

962
00:50:03,840 --> 00:50:06,910
It's impossible for this round
to have a straight.

963
00:50:07,110 --> 00:50:09,240
The moment I show him my three,

964
00:50:09,680 --> 00:50:11,850
"He must've put the card facing down..."

965
00:50:11,910 --> 00:50:13,180
"because he's aiming for a straight."

966
00:50:13,220 --> 00:50:15,580
I need to psychologically attack him
that way,

967
00:50:15,780 --> 00:50:17,850
but it's impossible to do that
with these cards.

968
00:50:18,020 --> 00:50:24,260
(He can't trick Seong Beom
into thinking about a straight option.)

969
00:50:27,030 --> 00:50:30,370
So I had no choice but to show him a two.

970
00:50:31,230 --> 00:50:32,470
Please...

971
00:50:32,470 --> 00:50:35,040
Please choose two. I prayed.

972
00:50:35,570 --> 00:50:36,570
Choose two.

973
00:50:36,570 --> 00:50:37,970
This is up to fate.

974
00:50:37,970 --> 00:50:39,370
The dice has been cast.

975
00:50:39,780 --> 00:50:42,280
Heo Seong Beom. Please choose a card.

976
00:50:46,720 --> 00:50:48,680
Another thing I thought was important...

977
00:50:48,680 --> 00:50:51,090
in Choice Hold'em...

978
00:50:51,220 --> 00:50:54,360
was the psychology of deciding
which card to face up or down.

979
00:50:55,190 --> 00:50:56,760
Most people...

980
00:50:57,090 --> 00:51:00,630
would put the card they don't want
the opponent to take...

981
00:51:00,630 --> 00:51:02,600
facing down.

982
00:51:02,730 --> 00:51:05,430
They'd place whatever looks appealing
face up.

983
00:51:05,770 --> 00:51:07,570
I saw the two facing up,

984
00:51:07,740 --> 00:51:10,240
and if I'd taken it,
I would've made a two pair.

985
00:51:11,370 --> 00:51:14,010
But for some reason,

986
00:51:14,180 --> 00:51:15,980
I wanted to take the one facing down.

987
00:51:17,710 --> 00:51:19,680
I kept glancing,

988
00:51:19,750 --> 00:51:21,650
and he was thinking for a very long time.

989
00:51:22,020 --> 00:51:23,450
I wondered...

990
00:51:23,450 --> 00:51:25,050
why he took so long to think.

991
00:51:25,050 --> 00:51:26,460
Thinking about that...

992
00:51:26,460 --> 00:51:27,860
made my forearm muscles ache.

993
00:51:28,460 --> 00:51:32,060
"Seong Beom, please be dumb and take two."

994
00:51:32,430 --> 00:51:34,130
"Let's end this in the sixth round."

995
00:51:34,130 --> 00:51:35,300
"Please."

996
00:51:37,370 --> 00:51:40,140
(After thinking for a long time,
he picks a card.)

997
00:51:40,340 --> 00:51:43,370
Heo Seong Beom, please reveal your hand.

998
00:51:45,970 --> 00:51:48,140
Heo Seong Beom, a triple of three.

999
00:51:48,140 --> 00:51:49,180
(He chose the card facing down.)

1000
00:51:50,250 --> 00:51:52,250
YunB, a pair of three.

1001
00:51:52,510 --> 00:51:55,080
Heo Seong Beom has won Round Six.

1002
00:51:55,080 --> 00:51:57,190
(Seong Beom makes himself back
from the death's door.)

1003
00:51:58,850 --> 00:52:02,560
Life doesn't go as planned.

1004
00:52:03,060 --> 00:52:05,560
The deity of victory,

1005
00:52:05,560 --> 00:52:07,300
the deity of poker, advented...

1006
00:52:07,300 --> 00:52:08,700
to help Seong Beom.

1007
00:52:09,230 --> 00:52:10,870
He made a bet because he had no choice,

1008
00:52:10,870 --> 00:52:13,200
and he won with a three of a kind.

1009
00:52:13,200 --> 00:52:14,470
Good job, Seong Beom.

1010
00:52:16,300 --> 00:52:18,710
We will begin Round Seven now.

1011
00:52:20,240 --> 00:52:22,240
Here are the community cards.

1012
00:52:22,240 --> 00:52:24,710
(Community card: 2, 2, 4)

1013
00:52:24,710 --> 00:52:26,850
We will proceed with the first bet.

1014
00:52:27,580 --> 00:52:29,580
Heo Seong Beom, place your bet.

1015
00:52:29,750 --> 00:52:32,450
(It's a triple of 2 now.)

1016
00:52:35,260 --> 00:52:36,290
(Heo Seong Beom bets 2 chips.)

1017
00:52:36,290 --> 00:52:38,760
You have bet two chips.

1018
00:52:40,560 --> 00:52:42,360
YunB has folded.

1019
00:52:43,030 --> 00:52:45,370
We will begin Round Eight now.

1020
00:52:45,370 --> 00:52:47,940
(Round 8, YunB: 22, Heo Seong Beom: 16)

1021
00:52:47,940 --> 00:52:50,270
You have bet two chips.

1022
00:52:50,370 --> 00:52:52,340
Heo Seong Beom has folded.

1023
00:52:52,740 --> 00:52:54,440
What I felt
while playing Choice Hold'em is...

1024
00:52:54,980 --> 00:52:59,210
that when there's a high chance
of the opponent having a good hand,

1025
00:52:59,410 --> 00:53:01,720
I shouldn't bet along.

1026
00:53:02,080 --> 00:53:04,450
When the opponent seemed
to have high-numbered cards,

1027
00:53:04,520 --> 00:53:06,790
I compared it with mine and folded a lot.

