1694
01:26:40,630 --> 01:26:42,240
Round Three of the final match...

1695
01:26:43,070 --> 01:26:44,640
(Card Chess)

1696
01:26:44,640 --> 01:26:46,870
is Card Chess.

1697
01:26:47,910 --> 01:26:51,810
Card Chess is a strategy game
in which players use cards...

1698
01:26:52,010 --> 01:26:54,380
with different movement rules
to move their pieces.

1699
01:26:55,280 --> 01:26:58,120
The game board consists of 25 squares...

1700
01:26:58,450 --> 01:27:00,420
arranged in a 5-by-5 grid,

1701
01:27:00,550 --> 01:27:03,120
and each player uses five pieces...

1702
01:27:03,120 --> 01:27:05,090
with distinct front and back sides.

1703
01:27:05,760 --> 01:27:08,460
Each player's five pieces are placed...

1704
01:27:08,560 --> 01:27:11,130
on the first row of the board,
all facing forward.

1705
01:27:12,370 --> 01:27:14,900
There are five cards used in the game.

1706
01:27:15,340 --> 01:27:16,370
Before the game begins,

1707
01:27:16,370 --> 01:27:20,270
the 2nd player places
2 of the 5 cards in front of himself,

1708
01:27:20,610 --> 01:27:22,240
while 2 of the remaining 3 cards...

1709
01:27:22,240 --> 01:27:24,080
are placed in front of the first player.

1710
01:27:25,040 --> 01:27:27,610
The remaining card
is placed in the waiting zone.

1711
01:27:28,820 --> 01:27:30,250
Once the cards have been placed,

1712
01:27:30,250 --> 01:27:33,150
players take turns,
starting with the first player.

1713
01:27:33,820 --> 01:27:36,190
First, the player chooses
1 of the 2 cards...

1714
01:27:36,190 --> 01:27:38,460
placed in front of him...

1715
01:27:38,790 --> 01:27:40,730
and moves one of their pieces...

1716
01:27:40,960 --> 01:27:43,060
according to the movement rules
on that card.

1717
01:27:43,930 --> 01:27:46,600
The card used is then moved
to the waiting zone,

1718
01:27:47,070 --> 01:27:49,400
and the card that was
previously in the waiting zone...

1719
01:27:49,570 --> 01:27:51,040
is taken and placed
in front of the player.

1720
01:27:51,900 --> 01:27:54,670
The movement rules for each card
are as follows.

1721
01:27:55,680 --> 01:27:58,210
For the Rook Card,
the piece can move one square...

1722
01:27:58,210 --> 01:27:59,650
in any of the four cardinal directions.

1723
01:27:59,650 --> 01:28:00,880
(Rook)

1724
01:28:01,080 --> 01:28:03,820
For the Bishop Card,
the piece can move one square...

1725
01:28:03,820 --> 01:28:05,180
in any of the four diagonal directions.

1726
01:28:06,190 --> 01:28:08,920
For the Attacker Card,
the piece can move...

1727
01:28:09,060 --> 01:28:10,620
up to two squares straight ahead
in the direction it is facing,

1728
01:28:10,620 --> 01:28:13,560
or one square diagonally
in either direction.

1729
01:28:14,160 --> 01:28:16,860
It cannot jump over other pieces.

1730
01:28:17,700 --> 01:28:20,800
When a piece reaches
the last row of the board,

1731
01:28:20,870 --> 01:28:23,170
it turns around
to face the opposite direction.

1732
01:28:24,200 --> 01:28:26,610
For the Knight Card,
the piece moves two squares straight...

1733
01:28:26,610 --> 01:28:28,140
in any of the four cardinal directions,

1734
01:28:28,140 --> 01:28:31,210
then one square
in either perpendicular direction.

1735
01:28:31,910 --> 01:28:34,410
It can jump over other pieces...

1736
01:28:34,410 --> 01:28:35,950
along its path.

1737
01:28:36,850 --> 01:28:40,690
For the Jumper Card, the piece can move
by jumping over another piece...

1738
01:28:40,950 --> 01:28:43,020
only when there is another piece
in 1 of the 8 surrounding squares.

1739
01:28:44,120 --> 01:28:47,590
If only two pieces remain on the board,

1740
01:28:47,990 --> 01:28:51,560
the Jumper Card immediately changes
into a Queen Card.

1741
01:28:52,400 --> 01:28:54,730
For the Queen Card,
the piece can move one square...

1742
01:28:54,730 --> 01:28:57,140
in any of the 4 cardinal
or 4 diagonal directions.

1743
01:28:58,270 --> 01:29:01,070
If an opponent's piece is on the square
where the piece lands,

1744
01:29:01,440 --> 01:29:03,110
the opponent's piece is removed
from the board.

1745
01:29:03,410 --> 01:29:04,580
The first player to successfully remove...

1746
01:29:04,580 --> 01:29:07,550
all of their opponent's pieces,

1747
01:29:08,150 --> 01:29:09,820
or place one of their own pieces...

1748
01:29:09,980 --> 01:29:13,190
on the opponent's castle square,
and keep it there for one full turn...

1749
01:29:13,450 --> 01:29:15,120
wins the set.

1750
01:29:15,990 --> 01:29:18,290
The game is played
over a maximum of three sets,

1751
01:29:18,690 --> 01:29:20,690
and the 1st player to win 2 sets...

1752
01:29:20,890 --> 01:29:23,630
becomes the final winner of Bloody Game X.

1753
01:29:24,730 --> 01:29:27,170
