I really want to win,

1777
01:30:23,590 --> 01:30:26,730
so I deliberately steered things
so that chess would come up in the final.

1778
01:30:27,360 --> 01:30:28,860
Things went according to what I intended.

1779
01:30:29,660 --> 01:30:32,770
I'm not sure how good YunB is at chess,

1780
01:30:33,030 --> 01:30:36,140
but I think it'll be hard for him
to beat me.

1781
01:30:36,840 --> 01:30:38,370
And when I was in grade four,

1782
01:30:39,570 --> 01:30:42,410
I retired from chess at the age of ten.

1783
01:30:44,480 --> 01:30:45,510
Well done.

1784
01:30:47,080 --> 01:30:48,110
Thank you.

1785
01:30:48,250 --> 01:30:49,850
You're one amazing guy.

1786
01:30:51,250 --> 01:30:52,690
He's really cute.

1787
01:30:53,190 --> 01:30:56,760
Like a puppy soaked in fear and rain,

1788
01:30:57,160 --> 01:30:58,860
he was trembling.

1789
01:30:59,230 --> 01:31:01,360
After participating
in various survival shows,

1790
01:31:02,230 --> 01:31:05,670
the most important thing, one that's
more important than the game itself,

1791
01:31:06,330 --> 01:31:07,470
is your mental strength.

1792
01:31:07,670 --> 01:31:09,140
I play chess too.

1793
01:31:09,140 --> 01:31:10,400
- You do?
- Yes.

1794
01:31:10,400 --> 01:31:11,970
I may not have joined
an international chess tournament,

1795
01:31:12,470 --> 01:31:13,470
Okay.

1796
01:31:13,470 --> 01:31:15,510
but I'm the best player in Bangbae-dong,
my neighborhood.

1797
01:31:16,080 --> 01:31:18,280
Okay. Number one player in Bangbae-dong.

1798
01:31:18,340 --> 01:31:20,250
- I'm the best player in Bangbae-dong.
- Okay.

1799
01:31:20,610 --> 01:31:23,980
When I first met YunB,
he didn't come off as a smart guy.

1800
01:31:24,150 --> 01:31:25,350
But the look in his eyes
was something else.

1801
01:31:25,350 --> 01:31:26,350
Honestly,

1802
01:31:27,590 --> 01:31:29,360
I thought I could beat him easily,

1803
01:31:29,860 --> 01:31:31,260
but I realized it could be hard.

1804
01:31:31,620 --> 01:31:34,760
It could be neck and neck.

1805
01:31:34,930 --> 01:31:36,230
But I think I'll be a bit better.

1806
01:31:36,800 --> 01:31:39,100
Now, we'll begin the first set.

1807
01:31:39,430 --> 01:31:41,970
Ji Hoo, decide if you'll go 1st or 2nd.

1808
01:31:43,040 --> 01:31:44,140
I'll go first.

1809
01:31:45,040 --> 01:31:47,270
In turn-based strategy games like this,

1810
01:31:47,370 --> 01:31:49,210
the first player usually has an advantage.

1811
01:31:49,380 --> 01:31:52,140
The second player could have an advantage
if they make a really strong setup,

1812
01:31:52,850 --> 01:31:54,780
but I couldn't come up with one.

1813
01:31:54,980 --> 01:31:57,650
If I couldn't come up with one,
then YunB wouldn't be able to either.

1814
01:31:57,650 --> 01:31:59,090
That's why I decided to go first.

1815
01:31:59,750 --> 01:32:01,950
The first player is Ji Hoo,

1816
01:32:02,260 --> 01:32:04,260
and the second player is YunB.

1817
01:32:04,460 --> 01:32:06,960
YunB, please place the two cards
you'll use...

1818
01:32:06,960 --> 01:32:08,860
in front of you.

1819
01:32:14,870 --> 01:32:16,100
(Rook, Bishop, Attacker...)

1820
01:32:16,100 --> 01:32:22,810
(Rook, Bishop, Attacker, Knight, Jumper)

1821
01:32:28,080 --> 01:32:31,320
As for Choice Hold'em,
I thought going first...

1822
01:32:31,480 --> 01:32:34,550
had a big advantage...

1823
01:32:34,550 --> 01:32:36,660
because you can figure out
what your opponent is thinking fast.

1824
01:32:36,660 --> 01:32:39,460
But for this game,
it's a lot better to go second.

1825
01:32:39,460 --> 01:32:40,860
If you're the second player,

1826
01:32:40,960 --> 01:32:44,130
you have to figure out
the rules of the cards fast,

1827
01:32:44,300 --> 01:32:47,000
but you can build your card deck
to your advantage.

1828
01:32:53,640 --> 01:32:57,410
(Passing the Rook Card and Jumper Card)

1829
01:33:02,450 --> 01:33:04,120
(Bishop, Attacker)

1830
01:33:04,120 --> 01:33:05,720
(Rook, Jumper)

1831
01:33:05,720 --> 01:33:08,450
I gave Ji Hoo the cards whose effect...

1832
01:33:08,450 --> 01:33:11,560
was the most unpredictable.

1833
01:33:12,330 --> 01:33:16,330
I built my deck around cards
that are most similar to chess...

1834
01:33:16,600 --> 01:33:19,370
and relatively easy to understand.

1835
01:33:19,570 --> 01:33:21,200
First player, Ji Hoo,

1836
01:33:21,200 --> 01:33:23,570
please choose a card
and move one of your pieces.

1837
01:33:33,880 --> 01:33:37,720
Actually, it was pretty easy
to think through the 1st and 2nd moves.

1838
01:33:38,150 --> 01:33:39,450
But it became really hard
to think of the next moves.

1839
01:33:39,450 --> 01:33:41,320
While I make the 1st and 2nd moves,

1840
01:33:41,550 --> 01:33:43,860
how will YunB make his moves?
It was really hard to predict.

1841
01:33:45,420 --> 01:33:46,830
There were just too many possible moves.

1842
01:33:47,530 --> 01:33:51,400
I thought about how I could create
the optimal setup, initiate a battle,

1843
01:33:51,900 --> 01:33:53,300
and gain a material advantage.

1844
01:33:54,470 --> 01:33:58,370
(Advancing one square with the Rook Card)

1845
01:33:59,970 --> 01:34:02,980
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Rook Card.

1846
01:34:03,580 --> 01:34:06,080
I moved the piece in the center
one square forward...

1847
01:34:06,580 --> 01:34:09,180
to take control of the center.

1848
01:34:09,720 --> 01:34:11,080
It's your turn, YunB.

1849
01:34:25,870 --> 01:34:27,100
(Advancing one square diagonally
with the Bishop Card)

1850
01:34:27,100 --> 01:34:30,170
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Bishop Card.

1851
01:34:30,440 --> 01:34:32,670
Ji Hoo didn't have the Attacker Card,

1852
01:34:32,840 --> 01:34:34,510
so he couldn't attack me.

1853
01:34:34,510 --> 01:34:37,140
That's why I thought my move served
both offensive and defensive purposes.

1854
01:34:37,940 --> 01:34:41,050
YunB moved his piece to the center
using the Bishop Card.

1855
01:34:41,210 --> 01:34:44,380
I thought the game
could be harder than I thought.

1856
01:34:44,850 --> 01:34:46,190
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

1857
01:34:56,900 --> 01:34:58,030
(Moving the piece to the center
using the Jumper Card)

1858
01:34:58,030 --> 01:35:01,000
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Jumper Card.

1859
01:35:01,300 --> 01:35:02,670
It's your turn, YunB.

1860
01:35:12,710 --> 01:35:15,380
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Rook Card.

1861
01:35:15,680 --> 01:35:17,180
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

1862
01:35:20,720 --> 01:35:24,020
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Bishop Card.

1863
01:35:24,960 --> 01:35:26,360
It's your turn, YunB.

1864
01:35:39,000 --> 01:35:40,010
Take this.

1865
01:35:41,270 --> 01:35:44,240
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Jumper Card.

1866
01:35:44,240 --> 01:35:46,080
(YunB has moved
within the Knight Card's range.)

1867
01:35:46,080 --> 01:35:47,950
The biggest advantage
of the Jumper Card...

1868
01:35:47,950 --> 01:35:50,580
is that it allows you
to cover a lot of ground.

1869
01:35:50,580 --> 01:35:53,550
I used the Jumper Card
to infiltrate Ji Hoo's side.

1870
01:35:53,550 --> 01:35:57,790
Actually, that was me provoking him.

1871
01:35:58,190 --> 01:35:59,460
"Let's duke it out."

1872
01:35:59,730 --> 01:36:02,630
It was a really good chance
to throw him off mentally.

1873
01:36:04,160 --> 01:36:06,570
Actually, that move...

1874
01:36:07,230 --> 01:36:08,430
I didn't expect it at all.

1875
01:36:09,440 --> 01:36:12,140
I was going to feel him out at first...

1876
01:36:12,540 --> 01:36:13,940
and outbox him.

1877
01:36:14,010 --> 01:36:15,440
I was going to keep my distance,

1878
01:36:15,440 --> 01:36:19,180
land a punch, dodge one,
and then strike again.

1879
01:36:19,480 --> 01:36:20,780
That was my plan.

1880
01:36:21,010 --> 01:36:23,380
But he came at me,
provoking me to punch him.

1881
01:36:24,650 --> 01:36:26,220
I couldn't avoid the fight any longer.

1882
01:36:26,350 --> 01:36:27,850
I have to enter the Dark Forest,

1883
01:36:28,120 --> 01:36:29,790
but there are three different paths
I can take.

1884
01:36:30,220 --> 01:36:32,020
The 1st path out of 3.

1885
01:36:32,630 --> 01:36:36,530
If I use the Knight Card on the piece
on B2 to capture his piece on C4,

1886
01:36:36,900 --> 01:36:40,270
he can then use his piece on C5
to capture mine,

1887
01:36:40,770 --> 01:36:42,170
using the Attacker Card.

1888
01:36:43,000 --> 01:36:44,070
He could capture my piece
using the piece on D3,

1889
01:36:44,070 --> 01:36:45,070
using the Bishop Card.

1890
01:36:45,940 --> 01:36:47,840
He could use the piece on D3
using the Bishop Card...

1891
01:36:47,840 --> 01:36:49,780
to capture my piece on C2.

1892
01:36:50,540 --> 01:36:53,080
He could use the Attacker Card,
instead of the Bishop Card.

1893
01:36:54,010 --> 01:36:55,250
And then...

1894
01:36:55,310 --> 01:36:57,020
he could use the piece on D3
using the Attacker Card...

1895
01:36:57,020 --> 01:36:58,720
to capture the piece on D1.

1896
01:36:59,390 --> 01:37:02,420
So I looked into the 1st possible move
out of 3,

1897
01:37:02,790 --> 01:37:04,420
and that branched out
into five possible moves.

1898
01:37:05,620 --> 01:37:07,130
My head was going to explode.

1899
01:37:10,660 --> 01:37:11,800
Should I move it or not?

1900
01:37:14,600 --> 01:37:17,240
Come on,
Mr. International Tournament winner.

1901
01:37:18,740 --> 01:37:21,070
Come on, Mr. International Champion.

1902
01:37:23,880 --> 01:37:25,410
Come on, Mr. KAIST.

1903
01:37:38,020 --> 01:37:41,330
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Knight Card.

1904
01:37:41,630 --> 01:37:43,660
YunB's piece has been removed.

1905
01:37:44,260 --> 01:37:47,300
It came down to whether
I struck first with my left or my right.

1906
01:37:47,800 --> 01:37:50,640
In the end, it didn't make much
of a difference when I just threw punches.

1907
01:37:50,640 --> 01:37:52,740
All right. The brawl is on.

1908
01:37:53,070 --> 01:37:54,370
It's your turn, YunB.

1909
01:37:58,540 --> 01:38:01,780
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Bishop Card.

1910
01:38:02,150 --> 01:38:04,050
Ji Hoo's piece has been removed.

1911
01:38:04,380 --> 01:38:05,650
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

1912
01:38:07,720 --> 01:38:08,750
Okay.

1913
01:38:10,220 --> 01:38:13,190
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Jumper Card.

1914
01:38:13,790 --> 01:38:15,660
YunB's piece has been removed.

1915
01:38:16,560 --> 01:38:17,930
It's your turn, YunB.

1916
01:38:23,500 --> 01:38:26,270
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Attacker Card.

1917
01:38:26,510 --> 01:38:28,270
Ji Hoo's piece has been removed.

1918
01:38:28,840 --> 01:38:30,180
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

1919
01:38:33,510 --> 01:38:36,420
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Bishop Card.

1920
01:38:36,750 --> 01:38:38,720
YunB's piece has been removed.

1921
01:38:39,290 --> 01:38:42,520
(3 black pieces were removed
in an instant.)

1922
01:38:42,520 --> 01:38:45,960
(2 black pieces versus 3 white pieces)

1923
01:38:46,530 --> 01:38:47,890
It's your turn, YunB.

1924
01:39:01,110 --> 01:39:04,010
I decided to pull back
and reset the situation.

1925
01:39:06,980 --> 01:39:09,950
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Knight Card.

1926
01:39:10,550 --> 01:39:12,220
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

1927
01:39:13,520 --> 01:39:15,320
YunB stepped back right then.

1928
01:39:15,790 --> 01:39:17,160
If you step back,

1929
01:39:17,420 --> 01:39:19,160
you're guaranteed to take a hit
before stepping back.

1930
01:39:19,360 --> 01:39:21,730
Because you're backing off
when it's your turn to strike.

1931
01:39:21,960 --> 01:39:23,830
That means I don't have to hurry at all.

1932
01:39:24,030 --> 01:39:26,900
If I hurry
just to finish the round quickly,

1933
01:39:26,900 --> 01:39:28,100
that'd be a losing move.

1934
01:39:28,370 --> 01:39:31,000
So I'll slowly close in,
gradually gaining ground...

1935
01:39:31,000 --> 01:39:32,370
by leveraging my numerical advantage.

1936
01:39:36,640 --> 01:39:39,580
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Rook Card.

1937
01:39:40,350 --> 01:39:41,880
It's your turn, YunB.

1938
01:39:46,420 --> 01:39:49,320
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Bishop Card.

1939
01:39:50,090 --> 01:39:52,560
I landed on the castle square
using the Bishop Card.

1940
01:39:52,860 --> 01:39:56,730
This setup itself
is a very defensive strategy.

1941
01:39:57,000 --> 01:39:58,860
"Let's see how you play from here."

1942
01:39:59,030 --> 01:40:00,670
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

1943
01:40:02,300 --> 01:40:05,900
Now, my opponent has built
a solid fortress in the corner.

1944
01:40:06,170 --> 01:40:08,940
Rather than entering the castle,
I need to surround it...

1945
01:40:08,940 --> 01:40:11,480
and force my opponent to come out.

1946
01:40:14,950 --> 01:40:16,920
So, using the Knight Card,

1947
01:40:22,090 --> 01:40:23,960
I moved my piece
right up to the castle gate,

1948
01:40:24,320 --> 01:40:27,630
forcing YunB to come out of the castle
by himself.

1949
01:40:28,290 --> 01:40:29,900
It's your turn, YunB.

1950
01:40:30,700 --> 01:40:35,130
(Rook, Jumper)

1951
01:40:48,550 --> 01:40:51,450
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Jumper Card.

1952
01:40:51,750 --> 01:40:53,350
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

1953
01:40:57,090 --> 01:40:59,060
My plan worked out exactly as intended,

1954
01:40:59,430 --> 01:41:00,930
forcing him to make a bad move.

1955
01:41:01,260 --> 01:41:04,300
And he moved his piece to the center
using the Jumper Card.

1956
01:41:04,760 --> 01:41:07,300
I made all his possible moves bad,

1957
01:41:07,470 --> 01:41:09,870
so he could only make a bad move,
breaking out of the castle by himself.

1958
01:41:10,200 --> 01:41:11,370
That's how I set up the play.

1959
01:41:11,640 --> 01:41:14,140
I'll be the one to survive
and make it out of the Dark Forest.

1960
01:41:17,240 --> 01:41:20,350
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Attacker Card.

1961
01:41:20,450 --> 01:41:22,710
I captured one of his pieces
using the Attacker Card.

1962
01:41:24,880 --> 01:41:28,350
I landed on the castle square
to avoid his attacks,

1963
01:41:28,350 --> 01:41:29,690
being defensive.

1964
01:41:29,790 --> 01:41:32,660
I think it was a losing move
to maintain that state one more time.

1965
01:41:34,630 --> 01:41:37,460
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Rook Card.

1966
01:41:37,530 --> 01:41:39,830
Ji Hoo's piece has been removed.

1967
01:41:40,430 --> 01:41:44,700
In the end, I was left
at a crushing 2-to-1 disadvantage.

1968
01:41:45,170 --> 01:41:46,670
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

1969
01:41:51,480 --> 01:41:54,680
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Bishop Card.

1970
01:41:54,880 --> 01:41:56,480
It's your turn, YunB.

1971
01:42:02,820 --> 01:42:05,690
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Knight Card.

1972
01:42:06,190 --> 01:42:07,790
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

1973
01:42:10,630 --> 01:42:12,970
There's a technique you can use
in the endgame of this game.

1974
01:42:19,270 --> 01:42:21,170
It's none other than passing
the Jumper Card to your opponent.

1975
01:42:21,770 --> 01:42:23,180
Most of the time,
the Jumper Card is used...

1976
01:42:23,180 --> 01:42:24,940
to jump over your own piece.

1977
01:42:25,110 --> 01:42:27,010
But when your opponent
has only one piece left,

1978
01:42:27,010 --> 01:42:29,150
you can't use the Jumper Card...

1979
01:42:29,350 --> 01:42:30,520
because he has only one piece.

1980
01:42:30,520 --> 01:42:32,680
There are four choices YunB can make.

1981
01:42:33,020 --> 01:42:35,720
Capturing my piece using
the Bishop Card or the Attacker Card,

1982
01:42:36,260 --> 01:42:37,760
capturing my piece in front
using the Attacker Card,

1983
01:42:37,990 --> 01:42:39,460
or retreating one square
using the Bishop Card.

1984
01:42:39,890 --> 01:42:41,130
There are four options.

1985
01:42:41,430 --> 01:42:43,030
For the three options
where YunB can capture my piece,

1986
01:42:43,430 --> 01:42:46,100
my two pieces are protecting
each other strongly with the Rook Card.

1987
01:42:46,670 --> 01:42:48,300
When one gets taken out,
I'm able to strike back right away.

1988
01:42:48,500 --> 01:42:50,000
Even if he retreats one space
with the Bishop Card,

1989
01:42:50,200 --> 01:42:51,770
I'm able to attack with my Knight.

1990
01:42:51,870 --> 01:42:53,670
All four of these situations...

1991
01:42:53,670 --> 01:42:56,580
led to a defeat the next turn.
It was a complete checkmate situation.

1992
01:42:57,440 --> 01:42:58,910
It's your turn, YunB.

1993
01:42:58,910 --> 01:43:00,580
(YunB: Attacker, Bishop,
Ji Hoo: Knight, Rook)

1994
01:43:00,580 --> 01:43:01,680
Oh, darn.

1995
01:43:11,720 --> 01:43:14,560
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Bishop Card.

1996
01:43:14,790 --> 01:43:16,460
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

1997
01:43:16,730 --> 01:43:18,030
Two.

1998
01:43:18,030 --> 01:43:21,030
(YunB: Attacker, Jumper,
Ji Hoo: Knight, Rook)

1999
01:43:23,100 --> 01:43:24,200
One.

2000
01:43:25,940 --> 01:43:28,410
All of YunB's pieces have been removed.

2001
01:43:28,740 --> 01:43:31,310
Kang Ji Hoo has won Set One.

2002
01:43:31,310 --> 01:43:33,680
(Kang Ji Hoo wins Set 1 in Card Chess.)

2003
01:43:36,210 --> 01:43:37,520
After getting his Knight,

2004
01:43:37,580 --> 01:43:40,220
Round 1 ends with the score of 2 to 0.

2005
01:43:40,390 --> 01:43:43,660
To be honest, I expected to win
5 to 0 or 4 to 0,

2006
01:43:43,820 --> 01:43:46,160
but it was a narrow win by just one piece.

2007
01:43:47,730 --> 01:43:48,830
I thought he was a tough opponent.

2008
01:43:48,860 --> 01:43:52,800
With this round,
including the card selection,

2009
01:43:52,800 --> 01:43:54,900
I was certain that I could do better
for the future rounds.

2010
01:43:54,900 --> 01:43:56,600
But a precious win...

2011
01:43:56,600 --> 01:44:00,370
was given away too easily.

2012
01:44:00,510 --> 01:44:04,210
I'm planning to be more offensive
in Round Two.

2013
01:44:04,640 --> 01:44:07,510
Now, we'll begin the second set.

2014
01:44:07,880 --> 01:44:10,820
YunB, decide if you'll go 1st or 2nd.

2015
01:44:17,020 --> 01:44:18,160
I'll go first.

2016
01:44:19,730 --> 01:44:21,990
YunB, you have decided to go first.

2017
01:44:22,630 --> 01:44:24,630
The reason I chose to go first...

2018
01:44:24,630 --> 01:44:28,330
was because I learned how big it was...

2019
01:44:28,330 --> 01:44:32,100
to take a piece first during Round One.

2020
01:44:32,100 --> 01:44:35,810
Ji Hoo, please place the cards
you'll use in front of you.

2021
01:44:45,750 --> 01:44:49,760
(Rook, Knight, Jumper, Attacker)

2022
01:44:49,760 --> 01:44:50,820
I have no idea.

2023
01:44:55,390 --> 01:44:56,430
After the first set,

2024
01:44:56,430 --> 01:44:59,670
I was able to see which cards were good.

2025
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:01,570
The Knight Card and Attacker Card...

2026
01:45:01,570 --> 01:45:04,500
were very strong as they could move
two spaces.

2027
01:45:04,500 --> 01:45:06,470
They can be used for long-range attacks.

2028
01:45:06,470 --> 01:45:10,080
The Bishop Card and Rook Card
can only move one space.

2029
01:45:10,140 --> 01:45:12,580
These cards were relatively weak.

2030
01:45:12,810 --> 01:45:15,480
They were cards that had to be used
to protect each other.

2031
01:45:15,750 --> 01:45:19,180
It's best to have both
the Knight Card and Attacker Card.

2032
01:45:19,380 --> 01:45:20,990
But even if I have both,

2033
01:45:21,390 --> 01:45:23,160
one of them has to be used right away.

2034
01:45:23,160 --> 01:45:24,620
I thought about...

2035
01:45:24,860 --> 01:45:27,460
how I could force my opponent
to give me...

2036
01:45:27,460 --> 01:45:28,460
both the Attacker Card
and the Knight Card.

2037
01:45:34,230 --> 01:45:36,470
Giving the Jumper Card
at the start was a way.

2038
01:45:36,940 --> 01:45:39,000
Since the pieces were standing
in a single file,

2039
01:45:39,000 --> 01:45:40,510
the Jumper Card couldn't be used.

2040
01:45:40,870 --> 01:45:43,480
If I give him the Jumper Card
and Attacker Card,

2041
01:45:43,610 --> 01:45:46,040
there will be a situation
when YunB is forced...

2042
01:45:46,040 --> 01:45:47,410
to use the Attacker Card.

2043
01:45:47,410 --> 01:45:49,080
All cards have been placed.

2044
01:45:49,080 --> 01:45:51,380
YunB will go first.

2045
01:46:01,430 --> 01:46:04,300
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Attacker Card.

2046
01:46:04,300 --> 01:46:05,330
(He moves one space forward
with the Attacker Card.)

2047
01:46:05,400 --> 01:46:07,000
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

2048
01:46:07,700 --> 01:46:09,130
Based on my strategy,

2049
01:46:09,130 --> 01:46:11,840
YunB had to use the Attacker Card.

2050
01:46:12,070 --> 01:46:15,170
He moved his piece in the middle
one space forward.

2051
01:46:15,170 --> 01:46:16,440
That was a good move.

2052
01:46:21,480 --> 01:46:24,450
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Bishop Card.

2053
01:46:25,220 --> 01:46:26,550
It's your turn, YunB.

2054
01:46:27,620 --> 01:46:31,620
Ji Hoo had both the Attacker Card
and the Knight Card.

2055
01:46:32,290 --> 01:46:34,630
Even if I had the center covered,

2056
01:46:35,060 --> 01:46:37,130
I was in a very bad spot.

2057
01:46:37,130 --> 01:46:39,660
Based on my guess,

2058
01:46:42,330 --> 01:46:44,270
I had to retreat.

2059
01:46:45,440 --> 01:46:48,510
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Rook Card.

2060
01:46:49,740 --> 01:46:52,010
Since he was an aggressive player,

2061
01:46:52,010 --> 01:46:54,080
I didn't expect him to retreat right away.

2062
01:46:54,380 --> 01:46:55,980
It was a play I didn't expect him to play.

2063
01:46:57,250 --> 01:47:00,090
I had two attack cards,

2064
01:47:00,550 --> 01:47:01,950
but they became useless.

2065
01:47:02,290 --> 01:47:04,890
Since he made a retreat,
he was out of my range.

2066
01:47:05,390 --> 01:47:08,760
I had to give up 1 of the 2.

2067
01:47:12,130 --> 01:47:15,270
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Knight Card.

2068
01:47:15,270 --> 01:47:16,370
(He uses his Knight Card.)

2069
01:47:16,370 --> 01:47:17,670
It's your turn, YunB.

2070
01:47:17,670 --> 01:47:19,170
(YunB's turn)

2071
01:47:23,280 --> 01:47:26,680
It's impossible for me to
go straight through.

2072
01:47:27,080 --> 01:47:29,750
The only way to strike...

2073
01:47:29,750 --> 01:47:32,080
is by hitting Ji Hoo's flanks.

2074
01:47:33,750 --> 01:47:36,120
I wondered how I could do that.

2075
01:47:47,930 --> 01:47:49,430
(He goes for the flank
with the Bishop Card.)

2076
01:47:49,430 --> 01:47:52,100
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Bishop Card.

2077
01:47:52,940 --> 01:47:54,470
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

2078
01:47:54,470 --> 01:47:56,040
(Ji Hoo's turn)

2079
01:47:56,040 --> 01:47:59,310
(YunB: Knight, Jumper,
Ji Hoo: Rook, Attacker)

2080
01:47:59,310 --> 01:48:01,810
While holding the Attacker Card,

2081
01:48:01,810 --> 01:48:04,280
my strategy was to focus
my pieces to the middle...

2082
01:48:04,280 --> 01:48:06,220
and charge at him.

2083
01:48:06,480 --> 01:48:09,820
The weakness of this strategy
was the flanks.

2084
01:48:10,020 --> 01:48:12,220
It's because the Attacker Card
can't move to the flanks.

2085
01:48:12,390 --> 01:48:14,860
"I didn't think about this."

2086
01:48:15,930 --> 01:48:17,000
"What should I do?"

2087
01:48:22,200 --> 01:48:23,200
Take it.

2088
01:48:28,910 --> 01:48:31,880
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Rook Card.

2089
01:48:31,880 --> 01:48:32,880
(He moves into the range
of the Knight Card.)

2090
01:48:32,880 --> 01:48:34,210
It's your turn, YunB.

2091
01:48:42,550 --> 01:48:45,590
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Knight Card.

2092
01:48:46,060 --> 01:48:47,890
Ji Hoo's piece has been removed.

2093
01:48:52,830 --> 01:48:55,930
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Bishop Card.

2094
01:48:56,200 --> 01:48:57,970
YunB's piece has been removed.

2095
01:48:58,370 --> 01:49:00,810
With an exchange of a piece,
YunB's flank strategy...

2096
01:49:00,810 --> 01:49:01,870
came to nothing.

2097
01:49:02,070 --> 01:49:04,580
My Spartan warriors
gathered in the middle...

2098
01:49:04,580 --> 01:49:05,710
were still strong.

2099
01:49:05,940 --> 01:49:07,350
It's your turn, YunB.

2100
01:49:07,350 --> 01:49:08,480
(YunB's turn)

2101
01:49:19,190 --> 01:49:21,760
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Rook Card.

2102
01:49:22,430 --> 01:49:25,730
Ji Hoo is taking control
of the center right now.

2103
01:49:26,160 --> 01:49:30,470
I planned to split my pieces
to both sides.

2104
01:49:30,470 --> 01:49:31,840
It was the scatter strategy.

2105
01:49:31,840 --> 01:49:35,270
YunB moved the Rook in the middle
to the right.

2106
01:49:35,710 --> 01:49:37,440
He split his pieces to both sides.

2107
01:49:37,580 --> 01:49:40,910
"Must I split my pieces
into two groups..."

2108
01:49:41,510 --> 01:49:43,450
"and hold a 2-on-2 battle?"

2109
01:49:44,050 --> 01:49:46,990
I wasn't able to use the strategy
I came up with up until now,

2110
01:49:47,720 --> 01:49:48,950
and my head was filled with thoughts.

2111
01:49:52,460 --> 01:49:55,660
But as YunB made this decision,
there was something that he gave up on.

2112
01:49:55,690 --> 01:49:56,900
It was the area in the middle.

2113
01:49:56,900 --> 01:49:59,130
"I must take the middle."

2114
01:50:03,340 --> 01:50:06,670
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Knight Card.

2115
01:50:07,340 --> 01:50:08,970
It's your turn, YunB.

2116
01:50:18,850 --> 01:50:20,950
Well, I have no choice.

2117
01:50:27,090 --> 01:50:29,890
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Bishop Card.

2118
01:50:29,890 --> 01:50:30,930
(He uses his Bishop Card.)

2119
01:50:32,900 --> 01:50:34,630
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

2120
01:50:35,130 --> 01:50:36,570
I realized this as soon as I saw the play.

2121
01:50:36,570 --> 01:50:37,700
This was a blunder.

2122
01:50:37,700 --> 01:50:39,100
YunB always has...

2123
01:50:39,100 --> 01:50:40,410
one out of four things
written on his face.

2124
01:50:40,970 --> 01:50:43,410
Guess, justification,

2125
01:50:43,740 --> 01:50:45,080
blunder, and reasonableness.

2126
01:50:45,440 --> 01:50:46,980
It's 1 out of those 4.

2127
01:50:47,580 --> 01:50:49,450
I was certain that it was a blunder,

2128
01:50:49,650 --> 01:50:51,620
but reasonableness
was written on his face.

2129
01:50:52,050 --> 01:50:55,420
"YunB must be thinking
that was reasonable."

2130
01:50:55,750 --> 01:50:57,920
I got a piece with the Rook Card.

2131
01:50:59,820 --> 01:51:01,860
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Rook Card.

2132
01:51:01,860 --> 01:51:03,460
YunB's piece has been removed.

2133
01:51:03,660 --> 01:51:05,030
YunB got my piece with his Knight Card.

2134
01:51:05,760 --> 01:51:07,600
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Knight Card.

2135
01:51:07,600 --> 01:51:09,470
Ji Hoo's piece has been removed.

2136
01:51:10,870 --> 01:51:12,800
The Attacker Card hidden behind
my Rook Card...

2137
01:51:12,800 --> 01:51:14,140
could be used for my win.

2138
01:51:14,340 --> 01:51:16,880
I think YunB missed the Attacker Card...

2139
01:51:16,880 --> 01:51:18,710
that was hidden behind the Rook Card.

2140
01:51:23,210 --> 01:51:26,280
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Attacker Card.

2141
01:51:26,990 --> 01:51:28,750
YunB's piece has been removed.

2142
01:51:29,450 --> 01:51:32,320
That was the biggest blunder in Round Two.

2143
01:51:32,760 --> 01:51:34,460
I missed it.

2144
01:51:34,930 --> 01:51:36,630
I missed that play.

2145
01:51:36,760 --> 01:51:39,060
I missed the Attacker
hidden behind the piece.

2146
01:51:40,900 --> 01:51:43,100
It felt like a hard hit
on the back of my head.

2147
01:51:44,400 --> 01:51:47,240
The card that I had was the Jumper Card.

2148
01:51:47,810 --> 01:51:51,740
What can I do with the Jumper Card?

2149
01:51:55,810 --> 01:51:58,580
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Jumper Card.

2150
01:51:58,580 --> 01:51:59,580
(YunB passes the Jumper Card for now.)

2151
01:51:59,980 --> 01:52:01,550
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

2152
01:52:07,560 --> 01:52:11,030
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Bishop Card.

2153
01:52:11,030 --> 01:52:13,000
YunB's piece has been removed.

2154
01:52:13,000 --> 01:52:14,370
It's your turn, YunB.

2155
01:52:18,870 --> 01:52:21,870
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Rook Card.

2156
01:52:22,140 --> 01:52:24,810
After another exchange of pieces,

2157
01:52:24,810 --> 01:52:25,940
it became 1 against 2.

2158
01:52:26,180 --> 01:52:30,050
The same ending as the first round
came upon me.

2159
01:52:30,380 --> 01:52:32,020
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

2160
01:52:36,750 --> 01:52:38,890
Chess is about understanding patterns.

2161
01:52:38,960 --> 01:52:40,690
Similar patterns keep appearing.

2162
01:52:40,990 --> 01:52:42,630
It's important to remember
the patterns seen before...

2163
01:52:42,630 --> 01:52:44,100
and to be able to use them.

2164
01:52:44,230 --> 01:52:46,970
The same pattern
as the Jumper Card checkmate pattern...

2165
01:52:46,970 --> 01:52:48,530
appeared to me.

2166
01:52:48,870 --> 01:52:51,300
To move the Jumper Card to him,

2167
01:52:51,300 --> 01:52:53,300
I stuck both of pieces together
with the Knight Card.

2168
01:52:57,840 --> 01:53:01,250
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Knight Card.

2169
01:53:02,110 --> 01:53:03,720
It's your turn, YunB.

2170
01:53:05,420 --> 01:53:08,050
Being 1 against 2 is the worst situation.

2171
01:53:08,320 --> 01:53:10,090
I could run away.

2172
01:53:10,490 --> 01:53:12,960
Or if I take 1 of Ji Hoo's 2 pieces,

2173
01:53:12,960 --> 01:53:15,260
the other one will always be there...

2174
01:53:15,590 --> 01:53:19,560
ready to slit my throat with a sword.

2175
01:53:39,980 --> 01:53:42,990
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Bishop Card.

2176
01:53:43,420 --> 01:53:45,020
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

2177
01:53:45,020 --> 01:53:47,960
(YunB: Knight, Attacker,
Ji Hoo: Jumper, Rook)

2178
01:53:52,000 --> 01:53:55,270
Ji Hoo, you moved your piece
using the Jumper Card.

2179
01:53:56,070 --> 01:53:57,700
It's your turn, YunB.

2180
01:53:57,700 --> 01:54:00,710
(YunB: Knight, Attacker,
Ji Hoo: Bishop, Rook)

2181
01:54:04,440 --> 01:54:05,540
There's only one option.

2182
01:54:10,850 --> 01:54:13,950
YunB, you moved your piece
using the Attacker Card.

2183
01:54:13,950 --> 01:54:15,650
It's your turn, Ji Hoo.

2184
01:54:27,200 --> 01:54:29,630
All of YunB's pieces have been removed.

2185
01:54:29,930 --> 01:54:32,800
Ji Hoo reaches two wins first.

2186
01:54:32,800 --> 01:54:34,070
(Ji Hoo reaches 2 wins first.)

2187
01:54:34,240 --> 01:54:35,310
Good game.

2188
01:54:36,070 --> 01:54:37,140
Thank you.

2189
01:54:38,510 --> 01:54:40,780
Round Three of the final match,
Card Chess.

2190
01:54:41,580 --> 01:54:43,850
Ji Hoo is the final winner.

2191
01:54:43,850 --> 01:54:45,550
(Ji Hoo wins Round 3 of the final match.)

2192
01:54:51,820 --> 01:54:55,090
The final match has come to an end.

2193
01:54:57,230 --> 01:55:00,100
The final winner of Bloody Game X...

2194
01:55:01,130 --> 01:55:02,930
is Kang Ji Hoo.

2195
01:55:02,930 --> 01:55:04,440
(Bloody Game X winner, Kang Ji Hoo)

2196
01:55:04,440 --> 01:55:06,070
- Gosh!
- Well done!

2197
01:55:34,470 --> 01:55:38,940
I feel so happy for Ji Hoo's win.

2198
01:55:39,300 --> 01:55:41,810
It was his first appearance
on Bloody Game.

2199
01:55:41,810 --> 01:55:43,740
The rookie becoming the champion...

2200
01:55:43,940 --> 01:55:47,010
meant a change of generation.

2201
01:55:47,150 --> 01:55:50,650
The champion title suits Ji Hoo perfectly.

2202
01:55:51,080 --> 01:55:54,350
That is why I'm satisfied with his win.

2203
01:55:55,990 --> 01:55:59,420
Bloody Game to me
is a survival game of life.

2204
01:55:59,420 --> 01:56:02,290
I believe Bloody Game
represents life itself.

2205
01:56:02,430 --> 01:56:05,000
I've been through all kinds of hardship,

2206
01:56:05,000 --> 01:56:07,870
and it was a tough ride.

2207
01:56:08,770 --> 01:56:12,970
(He started as a member of Team P2.)

2208
01:56:14,940 --> 01:56:19,310
(He got betrayed...)

2209
01:56:19,310 --> 01:56:22,450
(and was sent
to the outdoor survival grounds.)

2210
01:56:22,450 --> 01:56:24,680
I'm sure you're the only one
to peel garlic while wearing Thom Browne.

2211
01:56:25,350 --> 01:56:26,450
Exactly.

2212
01:56:26,980 --> 01:56:29,520
The team eliminated from
Bloody Game X is...

2213
01:56:29,990 --> 01:56:31,360
Team P2.

2214
01:56:33,660 --> 01:56:35,390
There wasn't a team...

2215
01:56:35,390 --> 01:56:37,630
that went through so much trouble...

2216
01:56:37,630 --> 01:56:40,670
and hardships like Team P2.

2217
01:56:40,670 --> 01:56:42,830
Team P2 got eliminated first,

2218
01:56:43,570 --> 01:56:46,570
but 2 members of Team P2
reached the final.

2219
01:56:47,470 --> 01:56:48,740
I feel proud about that.

2220
01:56:49,540 --> 01:56:53,680
This whole session
could feel long or short,

2221
01:56:53,810 --> 01:56:57,150
but I definitely feel alive
while being here.

2222
01:56:57,350 --> 01:57:01,190
Bloody Game is tough and exhausting,

2223
01:57:01,190 --> 01:57:04,560
but it's that stimulating and exciting.

2224
01:57:04,790 --> 01:57:06,020
Bloody Game is a place...

2225
01:57:06,020 --> 01:57:08,330
full of betrayal and warmth.

2226
01:57:09,390 --> 01:57:10,860
I grew more...

2227
01:57:10,860 --> 01:57:13,500
and showed more experience.

2228
01:57:13,500 --> 01:57:16,470
I feel really happy to have participated
in Bloody Game...

2229
01:57:16,470 --> 01:57:18,070
with those sides of me.

2230
01:57:18,270 --> 01:57:22,170
I've learned a lot once again
through Bloody Game X.

2231
01:57:23,810 --> 01:57:25,510
I'm so happy for you, Ji Hoo.

2232
01:57:25,740 --> 01:57:26,880
Thank you.

2233
01:57:28,450 --> 01:57:29,480
I feel great.

2234
01:57:29,910 --> 01:57:33,180
I feel really happy to have achieved...

2235
01:57:33,220 --> 01:57:36,790
the moment I really wished for.

2236
01:57:37,020 --> 01:57:39,290
The older members who have helped me...

2237
01:57:39,390 --> 01:57:42,160
must feel really proud...

2238
01:57:42,160 --> 01:57:43,730
to have raised me.

2239
01:57:44,100 --> 01:57:45,430
In my profile,

2240
01:57:45,530 --> 01:57:48,800
it says I'm a Presidential Scholar
of KAIST...

2241
01:57:49,470 --> 01:57:52,000
and the one who placed 3rd
in "Elite League 3."

2242
01:57:52,900 --> 01:57:56,240
"Am I here because I'm a great person?"

2243
01:57:56,440 --> 01:57:59,580
When I think about that,

2244
01:58:00,480 --> 01:58:01,550
that isn't the case.

2245
01:58:01,550 --> 01:58:03,920
I questioned everything on the first day.

2246
01:58:04,320 --> 01:58:06,550
I even doubted my team members.

2247
01:58:06,920 --> 01:58:09,090
- Right.
- Will you be able to handle that?

2248
01:58:09,690 --> 01:58:11,960
The older ones opened their hearts
to me first.

2249
01:58:12,020 --> 01:58:14,030
They treated me with genuine hearts.

2250
01:58:14,030 --> 01:58:15,760
I will transfer all funds to him.

2251
01:58:16,560 --> 01:58:18,130
Win. You must become the winner.

2252
01:58:18,730 --> 01:58:19,900
I will make sure to become the winner.

2253
01:58:20,630 --> 01:58:23,570
I didn't achieve this win
with my own abilities.

2254
01:58:24,100 --> 01:58:26,900
I must be humble and grateful.

2255
01:58:27,640 --> 01:58:29,310
The most memorable moment...

2256
01:58:29,840 --> 01:58:31,210
was when I lost my first family...

2257
01:58:32,580 --> 01:58:35,150
and my second family I got adopted into.

2258
01:58:36,050 --> 01:58:39,020
I cried my eyes out on the bed on my own.

2259
01:58:39,020 --> 01:58:41,390
I remember that moment the most.

2260
01:58:43,550 --> 01:58:45,860
"For a child to be raised properly,"

2261
01:58:45,860 --> 01:58:47,690
"the whole village must help."

2262
01:58:48,060 --> 01:58:49,630
There's this saying.

2263
01:58:49,630 --> 01:58:51,360
This isn't the Bloody Mansion.

2264
01:58:51,760 --> 01:58:53,400
This is the Mansion of Flesh and Blood.

2265
01:58:53,600 --> 01:58:56,400
This village was full of human charms...

2266
01:59:01,170 --> 01:59:04,580
that became my flesh and blood.

2267
01:59:05,810 --> 01:59:08,550
Soon, I will be the last one...

2268
01:59:09,450 --> 01:59:12,820
to leave this village.

2269
01:59:13,820 --> 01:59:15,650
I thought I was an adult,

2270
01:59:16,990 --> 01:59:17,990
but...

2271
01:59:18,960 --> 01:59:20,660
I deeply realized that...

2272
01:59:22,260 --> 01:59:23,790
I was still a child...

2273
01:59:25,700 --> 01:59:28,300
while being here.

2274
01:59:32,370 --> 01:59:36,240
I have many hills to climb.

2275
01:59:38,110 --> 01:59:39,410
I must grow a lot more...

2276
01:59:41,410 --> 01:59:44,080
to become an adult.

2277
01:59:44,750 --> 01:59:46,450
It was a short time,

2278
01:59:46,850 --> 01:59:49,790
but everyone here helped me...

2279
01:59:50,620 --> 01:59:52,460
for a whole week.

2280
01:59:53,120 --> 01:59:57,090
They helped me grow so much.

2281
01:59:58,830 --> 01:59:59,960
Even after leaving this place,

2282
02:00:00,930 --> 02:00:02,270
I will never forget...

2283
02:00:05,570 --> 02:00:06,800
the things I have received.

2284
02:00:08,040 --> 02:00:09,510
I will make sure to give more...

2285
02:00:11,240 --> 02:00:14,250
and become a great adult...

2286
02:00:15,910 --> 02:00:18,120
like the ones I've seen here.

2287
02:00:18,520 --> 02:00:22,490
With the prize money of 100,000 dollars,

2288
02:00:22,750 --> 02:00:24,960
I wish to donate it all to my alma mater,
KAIST,

2289
02:00:25,490 --> 02:00:28,390
for air-conditioning fees...

2290
02:00:29,390 --> 02:00:30,490
at the dorms.

2291
02:00:30,490 --> 02:00:32,230
It's really hot in the summer.

2292
02:00:32,830 --> 02:00:34,430
The air conditioners work,

2293
02:00:34,430 --> 02:00:36,670
but they don't feel cool at all.

2294
02:00:36,670 --> 02:00:39,970
Stress levels will go up
when it's too hot,

2295
02:00:39,970 --> 02:00:42,470
and that will be a hindrance
to their studies.

2296
02:00:42,870 --> 02:00:45,640
The talents of Korea
are struggling to study...

2297
02:00:45,940 --> 02:00:47,180
because of that.

2298
02:00:47,780 --> 02:00:51,480
That is why I wish to donate
all 100,000 dollars...

2299
02:00:51,850 --> 02:00:55,690
for air-conditioning fees
at the dorms of KAIST.

2300
02:04:22,030 --> 02:04:23,990
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
